BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Harvard Square Food & History Tour
DTSTART:20250913T000000
DTEND:20250913T020000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:7a34c2a9e0cd5947cb2015e62bbc15@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Do you know the "Cambridge" side of Harvard Square? Ever wonde
 r what Julia Child thought of her favorite neighborhood? Do you love old\,
  historic cities that have European cobblestone streets? Join us for a del
 icious culinary adventure through historical Harvard Square. You'll hear i
 nteresting stories about the Square\, learn fun facts about the restaurant
 s we visit\, and sample the best and most interesting food around -- and a
  lot of it. Located right outside of Boston on the Red Line MBTA Train Sto
 p\, Harvard Square is home to Harvard University but some guests are surpr
 ised to uncover its flourishing food scene with some of the best and most 
 unique food in the city. Harvard Square has deep roots in celebrating peop
 le from all walks of life\, and that diversity is reflected in its food of
 ferings. Music and live performance is a cornerstone of this cultural dist
 rict\, and we will spend time in the most honored performance halls in the
  city while learning about greats such as Joan Baez who was discovered her
 e. Each tour is 2 hours and includes 4 stops with plenty of food and less 
 than a mile of walking. We can't wait to take you on a unique\, foodie adv
 enture! While we can accommodate gluten-free options on our other tours\, 
 on this tour there is one stop where gluten-free substitutions are not ava
 ilable unfortunately. There is also two stops with dairy. Meet in front of
  Smith Campus Center (1350 Massachusetts Avenue\, Cambridge) Please note: 
 This location is outside of the Red Line MBTA right on Massachusetts Avenu
 e and across from Harvard Yard.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https
 ://www.meetboston.com/event/harvard-square-food-%26-history-tour/44162/
LOCATION:Off The Beaten Path Food Tours\, Harvard Square\, Cambridge\, MA
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/harvard-square-food-%26-history-tour/
 44162/
END:VEVENT
