BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Revolutionary Run
DTSTART:20251208T000000
DTEND:20251208T020000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:491e7e449f69837daa6e7cae684469@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Ready to experience Boston from a runner's perspective? Join u
 s for a guided running tour through some of the city's most iconic landmar
 ks\, all while soaking in the rich history and vibrant energy that make Bo
 ston such a unique place to explore. You'll hit must-see spots like the Bo
 ston Common\, the Boston Public Garden\, and the famed finish line of the 
 Boston Marathon\, while passing by picturesque views along the Charles Riv
 er Esplanade\, Beacon Hill\, and the world-famous Back Bay. This route cov
 ers the final leg of the Boston Marathon\, which gives you the chance to r
 un the same stretch where thousands have pushed through to complete the le
 gendary 26.2-mile race. Along the way\, we’ll make stops at scenic spots
  for photo ops and quick stretch breaks—perfect for both seasoned runner
 s and those looking to enjoy the sights at a comfortable pace. LEARN MORE 
 / BOOK A TOUR\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.
 com/event/a-revolutionary-run/88385/
LOCATION:City Fit Tours\, Boston Common 139 Tremont Street\, Boston\, MA
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/a-revolutionary-run/88385/
END:VEVENT
