BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BPL Studio Series
DTSTART:20260326T000000
DTEND:20260326T020000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:c54f745badf043c6a456ae5d50337b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:GBH offers a wide variety of in-person and virtual events. Fro
 m live music recordings\, lectures and screenings to our virtual Book Club
 \, tasting events and more\, stay connected to our community. Whatever you
 ’re interested in—news\, history\, the arts or music\, we’ve got you
  covered. Fill your calendar with this rich diversity of events and be ins
 pired\, informed and entertained. GBH Jazz Night with Sam Spear 5:30pm Thu
 \, May 14\, 2026 GBH Jazz Night with Tiger Okoshi: A Tribute to Miles Davi
 s 5:30pm Thu\, May 28\, 2026 Boston Public Radio LIVE at the Boston Public
  Library TUE\, WED\, FRI\, 11am-1pm On Tuesdays\, Wednesdays\, and Thursda
 ys\, Boston Public Radio turns the GBH Studio at the Boston Public Library
  into an arena for smart\, local conversation. Join veteran hosts Jim Brau
 de and Margery Eagan as they dive into the headlines with the leaders and 
 thinkers who are actively shaping life in New England. You can catch the s
 how live in person at the library\, or join the conversation from anywhere
  by texting\, calling\, or emailing the studio as the cameras roll. Whethe
 r you’re sitting front row in Copley Square or streaming the daily broad
 cast on YouTube\, it’s your go-to source for the debates and stories tha
 t define our community. The Culture Show LIVE at the Boston Public Library
  WED & FRI\, 2-3pm On Wednesdays and Fridays\, The Culture Show brings a h
 igh-energy vibe to the GBH Studio at the Boston Public Library\, diving in
 to the trends that shape our lives. Hosted by Executive Arts Editor Jared 
 Bowen alongside a rotating group of cultural correspondents\, the show dis
 sects everything from the latest Netflix drop and street style to the city
 's best food and theater. The Curiosity Desk LIVE at the Boston Public Lib
 rary (starting April 10) FRI\, 1-2pm Each Friday at the Boston Public Libr
 ary\, The Curiosity Desk takes a deep dive into the "why" behind the world
  we live in. Hosted by Edgar B. Herwick III\, the show explores everything
  from quirky local history to the profound mysteries of science and societ
 y. GBH Amplifies EVERY THURSDAY\, 12:30-1:30pm 1st Thursday: Hosted by Jam
 es “Jimmy” Hills\, Java with Jimmy 2nd Thursday: Hosted by Ron Mitchel
 l\, Bay State Banner 3rd Thursday: Hosted by Alberto Vasallo III\, El Mund
 o Boston 4th Thursday: Hosted by Tracy Chang\, Pagu Every Thursday\, GBH A
 mplifies transforms the GBH Studio at the Boston Public Library into a pre
 mier destination for live\, unfiltered community journalism. Rotating host
 s James “Jimmy” Hills\, Ron Mitchell\, Alberto Vasallo III\, and Tracy
  Chang take the mic to lead deep-dive conversations with the activists\, a
 rtists\, and local leaders who are moving the needle in Greater Boston. Wh
 ether you drop by Copley Square to join the live audience or stream the se
 ssions later\, you’ll experience a powerful exchange of ideas that eleva
 tes authentic local voices to a city-wide stage. Outspoken Saturdays FIRST
  SATURDAY of the month\, 2-3pm Hosted by award-winning activist and poet A
 manda Shea\, Outspoken Saturdays transforms the GBH Studio at the Boston P
 ublic Library into a vibrant monthly hub for contemporary spoken word. Thi
 s curated series brings together a diverse community of writers to share w
 ork ranging from deeply personal reflections to playful observations on ev
 eryday life. More than just a performance\, it serves as a vital anchor fo
 r Boston’s creative scene\, offering a space for the next generation of 
 poets to connect and experience the transformative power of live art. GBH 
 Jazz Nights SECOND THURSDAY of the month\, 5:30-7pm On the second Thursday
  of every month\, GBH Music and JazzBoston transform the GBH Studio at the
  Boston Public Library into the city’s premier scene for local jazz. Thi
 s curated residency highlights the incredible range of talent within the G
 reater Boston area\, offering an intimate look at the musicians shaping th
 e modern genre. It’s a sophisticated yet welcoming evening designed to c
 onnect a new generation of listeners with soulful\, world-class performanc
 es right in the heart of Copley Square. NOVA Science Trivia THIRD THURSDAY
  of the month\, 5:30-7pm Every month\, NOVA turns the GBH Studio at the Bo
 ston Public Library into a high-energy social spot for science enthusiasts
  with its signature trivia night. Whether you’re a space buff or a biolo
 gy nerd\, this event invites you to test your expertise across creative ca
 tegories ranging from the natural world to the frontiers of physics. It is
  the perfect atmosphere to meet a like-minded community\, win unique prize
 s\, and engage with complex topics in an approachable way.\n\nSources: Mee
 t Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/bpl-studio-series/8
 9816/
LOCATION:Boston Public Library\, GBH Studio at the Boston Public Library 7
 00 Boylston Street\, Boston\, MA\, 02116
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/bpl-studio-series/89816/
END:VEVENT
