 lled sushi every Wednesday night. Guests can choose from a selection of su
 shi and hand rolls alongside several sake offerings\, including a sake fli
 ght designed for exploring different styles. The name Shuden is a nod to t
 he lively clusters of bars and eateries found outside train stations throu
 ghout Japan. The concept also pays homage to Boston’s own railroad histo
 ry: the Boston & Albany Railroad once ran directly alongside The Lenox Hot
 el at the turn of the 20th century. LEARN MORE HERE\n\nSources: Meet Bosto
