BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bounty
DTSTART:20261002T000000
DTEND:20261231T000000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:3b9925059dd6c9e18f5de8ad3355bf@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:In Bounty \, Penobscot parents and children resist erasure and
  commemorate survival by reading and reacting to one of the dozens of gove
 rnment-issued bounty proclamations that motivated colonial settlers to hun
 t\, capture\, kill\, and scalp Indigenous people. Many of these laws were 
 signed in the room where this film was made\, the council chamber of the O
 ld State House. Scalping people for cash rewards and land is a devastating
  idea and shocking practice\, essential to how the United States became a 
 nation\, built on top of hundreds of Indigenous nations who thrived here f
 or millennia before Europeans invaded these shores. Bounty is a filmic tes
 timony of the immeasurable resistance and survivance of Indigenous Peoples
 . The film is the cornerstone of this media ecosystem which invites us all
  to face stories of the incalculable loss\, suffering\, and unacknowledged
  trauma inflicted upon Indigenous People by settlers\, past and present.\n
 \nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/bount
 y/93556/
LOCATION:Revolutionary Spaces - Old South Meeting House\, 310 Washington S
 treet\, Boston\, MA\, 02108
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/bounty/93556/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Freaky Tiki Cruise
DTSTART:20261002T000000
DTEND:20261031T000000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:a14708a987d8615d709c1f58d4299a@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The Beacon Tiki Boat has been overtaken. All October long\, ou
 r laid back island escape transforms into a floating haunted hideaway for 
 the Freaky Tiki Takeover. Step aboard and cruise the Charles River surroun
 ded by spooky decor\, flickering lights\, tropical tunes with a mischievou
 s twist and skyline views that look just a little more mysterious after su
 nset. Drinks are available for purchase from the onboard bar\, including l
 imited time specialty cocktails served in souvenir glasses. Costumes are e
 ncouraged. Bonus points for tiki meets terror. It is the same relaxed\, we
 lcoming tiki cruise you love\, just with a little extra bite. Meeting Loca
 tion Tiki Cruises depart from CambridgeSide Mall located at 100 CambridgeS
 ide Place Cambridge\, MA 02141. The boat and ticket booth are located outs
 ide the doors of the CanalSide Food Hall at the CambridgeSide Mall. Valida
 ted parking is available for $4.00 at the CambridgeSide Mall Garage Direct
 ions Drinks with a View The onboard Tiki bar is stocked with a selection o
 f canned beers\, wines\, and cocktails for purchase\, making it easy to gr
 ab a refreshing drink and settle in as you cruise along the river. Whether
  you are sipping slowly or celebrating with friends\, the bar is there to 
 keep the island vibes going from start to finish. Alongside our regular ba
 r menu\, October cruises feature limited edition Freaky Tiki cocktails des
 igned to summon your inner pirate. Featured drinks may include: Captains C
 urse - Mt Gay rum\, apple cider\, splash of ginger beer Stormy Seas - Ging
 er beer topped with Goslings dark rum Pirates Poison - Mt Gay rum\, pineap
 ple juice\, orange juice\, splash of grenadine Sirens scream - Apple cider
  topped with ginger beer Take a sneak peek at the menu before you cruise: 
 Here! Costumes Encouraged! Dress in costume (bonus points for tiki + terro
 r!)\, snap some pics onboard and we will share on social! Join us...if you
  dare! Highlights A floating tiki cruise with a Halloween twist Spooky dec
 or and themed island atmosphere Open air cruising with river breezes and s
 unshine\, plus weather protection when needed Scenic views of the Boston a
 nd Cambridge skyline from the water Onboard tiki bar with a trained barten
 der serving themed October cocktails Experienced captain and crew ensuring
  a smooth\, safe\, and enjoyable cruise Festive island inspired music sett
 ing the tone for the ride A welcoming experience for all ages\, from famil
 ies to friend groups Easy parking at the CambridgeSide Mall Garage for jus
 t $4 Cruises sail rain or shine so the good vibes keep rolling Schedule & 
 Ticket Prices Public Tiki Cruises October 1st - 31st\, 2026 Friday - Satur
 day: 90 Minute Tiki Cruise 3:00 pm\, 5:00pm\, & 7:00pm Adults: $40 Militar
 y/Student/Seniors: $37 Child Under 12: $35 LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS\n\nSou
 rces: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/freaky-tik
 i-cruise/93260/
LOCATION:Charles River Boat Company\, Charles River Boat Company 100 Cambr
 idgeSide Place\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02141
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/freaky-tiki-cruise/93260/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Mighty Mighty Bus Tour: Boston's Rock N Roll Past and Present
DTSTART:20261002T000000
DTEND:20261002T020000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:b6e4f5af2fef3c5adef2c04b3c5071@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:From historic Boston Common\, journey through Boston's rock 'n
 ' roll past with a local musician. See where iconic artists like Pixies\, 
 Joan Baez\, and The Cars lived\, recorded and performed. Dig for vinylat a
  local record storem explore harvard Square's folk roots\, and end up with
  a pint at an Irish pub. HIGHLIGHTS The Boston Common: America’s oldest 
 park and setting for numerous performances including the pioneering concer
 t series affectionally known as “Summer Thing”. The Theatre District/W
 ang: Home to many still active venues built during the early 20th century 
 including the Wang Theatre which is home to the recently established Folk 
 Americana Roots Hall of Fame. The Boston Tea Party: Original location of t
 he house of house of worship-turned psychedelic music venue that featured 
 the most impactful acts of its day including Led Zeppelin\, the Who\, Van 
 Morrison\, and the Velvet Underground. Storyville\, Jazz club owned by pia
 nist George Wein where legends such as Duke Ellington\, Dave Brubeck\, Bil
 ly Holiday\, Sarah Vaughn\, and Errol Garner played. Newbury St Bustling B
 ack Bay commercial stretch flanked by 19th century brownstones. Original h
 ome of Newbury Comics\, WBCN\, Berklee College of Music\, and Intermedia S
 tudios/Synchro Sound where Aerosmith\, Cars and many others recorded. Kenm
 ore Square Nexus of Boston’s underground and punk scene in the latter pa
 rt of the 20th century. Location of the Rat where numerous bands emerged o
 ut of in the 70s and 80s. Venue where Pixies first shared the same bill as
  the Throwing Muses. Central Square/The Middle East Upstairs Vibrant Cambr
 idge hub for musicians featuring an array of venues including The Middle E
 ast\, a key stepping stone for many post punk and alternative bands in the
  80/90s including Morphine\, Dinosaur Jr. Buffalo Tom\, Throwing Muses\, C
 ome\, Julianna Hatfield\, and the Mighty Mighty Bosstones. Harvard Square 
 Center of Folk Revival in New England and home to several venues including
  the Sinclair and legendary Club Passim where artists from Joan Baez to Tr
 acy Chapman got their start. McCarthy’s/Toad Restaurant and treasured li
 ve music venue. Host to daily musical events from Irish Seisuns to Rock ba
 nds. LEARN MORE / BUY TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https:/
 /www.meetboston.com/event/the-mighty-mighty-bus-tour%3a-bostons-rock-n-rol
 l-past-and-present/93523/
LOCATION:Boston Common Visitor Center\, Boston Common Visitor Center 139 T
 remont Street\, Boston\, MA
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-mighty-mighty-bus-tour%3a-bostons
 -rock-n-roll-past-and-present/93523/
END:VEVENT
