BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wistariahurst Museum\, Victorian Sentiments
DTSTART:20261027T173000
DTEND:20261027T183000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:9d8605e98dcb14762be2eeaac4f59e@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Wistariahurst Museum announces Victorian Sentiments\, a presen
 tation on mourning jewelry and grave iconography on October 27th at 5:30pm
 . This presentation corresponds with the museum’s current exhibit Mement
 o Mori on view in the gallery through November 3rd. This exhibit features 
 historic items relating to mourning from the collections of Wistariahurst 
 and the Longmeadow Historical Societly. Jewelry and gravestones may seem t
 o be an unlikely combination\, but both reflect society’s beliefs about 
 death and mourning in similar ways. Though we may identify mourning jewelr
 y and sentimental gravestone symbolism with the Victorian period\, their r
 oots and usage go back to antiquity: looking back just a few hundred years
  reveals dramatic changes in how people thought about death. Joanne and De
 nnis Picard of Westfield\, Massachusetts\, will share images and stories a
 bout the changes in our area with the coming of garden cemeteries and the 
 formal ritualization of mourning. This presentation will be held in Wistar
 iahurst Museum’s Music Room on Tuesday\, October 27th\, 5:30-6:30pm. Adm
 ission is donation-based\, with a sliding scale of $1 – $10. Register fo
 r this event\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://explore
 westernmass.com/event/wistariahurst-museum-victorian-sentiments/
LOCATION:Wistariahurst Museum\, 238 Cabot Street\, Holyoke\, MA\, 01040
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/wistariahurst-museum-victorian-se
 ntiments/
END:VEVENT
