UID:ad6aeda818c0e5de2105d957af7813@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join Wenham Museum for our annual event: Baby’s First Hallow
 een! Celebrate Halloween with a festive morning designed especially for li
 ttle ones and their grown-ups! Dress up in your favorite costume and enjoy
  not-so-spooky Halloween fun throughout Wenham Museum. Halloween Sensory P
 lay: Make your own pretend potions and explore themed sensory bins. Hands-
 On Crafts: Paint a mini pumpkin and decorate your own trick-or-treat bag. 
 Family Costume Photos: Visit our professional photographer for a fun famil
 y photo in your Halloween costumes! Photo sessions are free\, with photos 
 available for purchase. Costume Parade: Show off your Halloween look in a 
 festive parade through the Museum. Halloween Dance Party: Dance\, move\, a
 nd groove to kid-friendly Halloween music from 10:00 AM -10:30 AM Interact
 ive Exhibits: Explore Wenham Museum together and enjoy plenty of opportuni
 ties for hands-on play. Come dressed in costume and make some magical Hall
 oween memories with your little one! Activity fee: $14 General | $12 Membe
 rs | Children Under 1 Free Note: This fee covers participation in Baby’s
  First Halloween activities only. Museum admission is not included and mus
 t be purchased separately for guests who wish to explore the Museum’s ex
 hibits before\, during\, or after the event. Museum Admission: $14 Adults 
 & Children | $12 Seniors & Grandparents | Members Free | Children Under 1 
 Free All proceeds directly support Wenham Museum and help sustain our exhi
 bits\, educational programs\, and historical collections. Learn More: http
 s://www.wenhammuseum.org/event/babys-first-halloween-2/\n\nSources: North 
 of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/babys-first-hallowe
 en-2/
LOCATION:Wenham Museum\, 132 Main St.\, Route 1A\, Wenham\, MA\, 01984
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/babys-first-halloween-2/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BVCC's Business Leadership Summit Series: AI
DTSTART:20261028T000000
DTEND:20261028T000000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:7e9cdb78c20161ef63ad30dd673797@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The Blackstone Valley Chamber of Commerce (BVCC) is proud to a
 nnounce a quarterly leadership series exploring the forces reshaping busin
 esses. The inaugural summit will focus on Artificial Intelligence\, design
 ed for business owners\, executives and department leaders to make better 
 decisions about where AI belongs\, where it does not\, and where human jud
 gment still matters most. Leading Through the Age of AI\, will take place 
 on Wednesday\, October 28\, 2026\, from 8:00am-1:30pm\, at Blackstone Vall
 ey Chamber of Commerce\, located at 670 Linwood Avenue\, Suite 5\, Whitins
 ville\, MA 01588. This executive-level\, hands-on\, half-day summit will g
 ive you confidence in your decisions\, your team\, and your business. Join
 ing us will be two facilitators bringing different\, but complimentary per
 spectives to the conversation. Lynn Whitney-Turner\, Founder of CORE XP Bu
 siness Solutions\, will lead “Riding the Waves: Helping Leaders Navigate
  the Forces Changing Business.” Drawing from her experience participatin
 g in AI leadership summits and examining the forces reshaping today's busi
 ness environment\, Lynn will help leaders look beyond the technology itsel
 f and consider how they can lead effectively through rapid change. Her ses
 sion will focus on building clarity\, confidence and control\, particularl
 y for leaders who may already be using AI every day\, are skeptical of it
 \, or are somewhere in between. Kham Inthirath\, CEO of AI Advisor Guy\, w
 ho will take participants from conversation into application\, with a prac
 tical look at how AI can become part of the way they actually work. Rather
  than simply demonstrating another collection of AI tools\, Kham will help
  participants build an AI workspace and assistant around the way you work
 \, creating an experience that is relevant to your own workflow and respon
 sibilities. “This is a working summit\, not just a presentation\,” sai
 d Jeannie Hebert\, BVCC President & CEO. “We want our leaders to leave w
 ith something they can actually use. Whether they are just beginning to ex
 plore AI or already incorporating it into their daily work\, the goal is f
 or participants to return to their businesses with greater confidence\, a 
 clearer understanding of what matters\, and practical tools they can conti
 nue using.” To register\, please visit\, www.blackstonevalley.org/events
 . Pricing for Members is $199\, and $249 for Future Members. Business lead
 ers are encouraged to register early for the inaugural summit\, bring a la
 ptop\, and one real business challenge they face to be discussed. Coffee a
 nd lunch is included!\n\nSources: Discover Central Massachusetts\nEvent pa
 ge: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/bvccs-business-leadership-summ
 it-series%3a-ai/31081/
LOCATION:Blackstone Valley Chamber of Commerce\, 670 Linwood Ave #5\, Whit
 insville\, MA\, 01588
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/bvccs-business-leadership-summ
 it-series%3a-ai/31081/
END:VEVENT
