BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Eric Carle Museum\, Educators’ Night
DTSTART:20261028T153000
DTEND:20261028T183000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:72b11864e40cc0a507db04a089ab0f@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Educators’ Night: Jarrett J. Krosoczka & Dr. Catherine A. Sa
 nderson Free. Reservations are required. The Carle is pleased to welcome J
 arrett J. Krosoczka and Dr. Catherine A. Sanderson as the 2026 Educators
 ’ Night guest speakers. This event is free and open to all educators as 
 space permits. Reservations are required . Book signing to follow program.
  Can’t make the event? Order books online to reserve signed books at The
  Carle Bookshop. Schedule of events 3:30–4:30 pm Guests will have time t
 o browse the Museum\, enjoy light refreshments\, and collect free material
 s for their classroom. 4:30–5:30 pm Lecture followed by Q&A . 5:30–6:3
 0 pm Book signing and Museum exploration. We work to provide accessible pr
 ogramming. If you need accommodation to participate in this program\, plea
 se contact Natalie at programs@carlemuseum.org. We ask that requests are s
 ent at least five business days in advance of the program so we can make a
 rrangements. Thank you! Who You’ll Meet Jarrett J. Krosoczka Jarrett J. 
 Krosoczka is an award-winning\, New York Times bestselling author and illu
 strator of more than forty books for young readers\, including the graphic
  memoir Hey\, Kiddo \, a finalist for the National Book Award\, and its fo
 llow-up Sunshine . He also created the wildly popular Lunch Lady graphic n
 ovels and has written for Spider-Man \, Star Wars \, and Snoopy . Realizin
 g his books can inspire young readers beyond the page\, Krosoczka founded 
 the School Lunch Hero Day campaign and established a scholarship to fund a
 rt classes for underprivileged children in his hometown. Krosoczka and his
  family live in western Massachusetts.​​​​ Artist website Dr. Cath
 erine A. Sanderson Dr. Catherine Sanderson\, a Princeton and Stanford-educ
 ated psychologist\, is a sought-after keynote speaker and the Poler Family
  Professor of Psychology at Amherst College who delivers engaging\, resear
 ch-based talks that help audiences thrive at work and in life. She is the 
 author of The Positive Shift and Why We Act\, recorded the popular Introdu
 ction to Psychology course for The Great Courses\, and delivered a widely 
 viewed TED x talk on the Psychology of Inaction\, exploring why people sta
 y silent — and how to build moral courage in workplaces and communities.
  Website\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewest
 ernmass.com/event/the-eric-carle-museum-educators-night/
LOCATION:The Eric Carle Museum of Picture Book Art\, 125 W Bay Road\, Amhe
 rst\, MA\, 01002
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/the-eric-carle-museum-educators-n
 ight/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Music of Hey Arnold!
DTSTART:20261028T000000
DTEND:20261028T000000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:afb6a8064d31c10cd7085025639ee6@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The Music of Hey Arnold! Live featuring Jim Lang & The PS 118 
 AllStars celebrates the 30th anniversary of one of television's most cheri
 shed animated series. Led by award winning composer Jim Lang\, best known 
 for his unforgettable theme music\, original songs\, and score for Hey Arn
 old!\, this one of a kind concert brings the music of the series to life o
 n stage. Blending jazz\, hip hop\, blues\, R&B and funk\, Lang created a s
 ound unlike anything else on television\, helping give Hey Arnold! its hea
 rt\, warmth\, humor and soul. Thirty years later\, the music continues to 
 connect with fans of all ages and inspire musicians around the world. Perf
 ormed by Jim Lang and The PS 118 AllStars\, the evening features the show'
 s unforgettable themes\, fan favorite songs\, and some of the moments that
  made Hey Arnold! so special. Accompanied by multimedia visuals and storie
 s from behind the music\, the performance also includes a special guest ap
 pearance by series creator Craig Bartlett. Whether you grew up with Hey Ar
 nold! or are discovering its music for the first time\, this 30th annivers
 ary celebration is a chance to experience one of animation's most distinct
 ive and enduring scores performed live by the composer who created it.\n\n
 Sources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-mus
 ic-of-hey-arnold!/92806/
LOCATION:Chevalier Theatre\, 30 Forest Street\, Medford\, MA\, 02155
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-music-of-hey-arnold!/92806/
END:VEVENT
