BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toad The Wet Sprocket
DTSTART:20261028T000000
DTEND:20261028T000000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:d61471fd066e80462b3bf15d8711ba@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Few bands have earned the kind of devotion Toad the Wet Sprock
 et inspires. Since forming in Santa Barbara in 1986 — four friends\, Gle
 n Phillips\, Todd Nichols\, Dean Dinning\, and Randy Guss\, met in a high 
 school theater group and named themselves after a fictional Monty Python b
 and. The band has spent four decades making music that\, as Phillips himse
 lf puts it\, reaches toward the light even when there's shadow in it. Thei
 r debut album\, Bread & Circus \, recorded DIY-style in a tract home for j
 ust $600\, caught the attention of Columbia Records and launched a career 
 defined by an uncompromising independent spirit. That spirit paid off: Fea
 r (1991) went platinum and spawned top-20 hits “All I Want” and “Wal
 k on the Ocean\,” followed by a second platinum album\, Dulcinea (1994)
 \, featuring fan favorites “Fall Down” and “Windmills.” Their musi
 c became the soundtrack to a generation — turning up in Buffy the Vampir
 e Slayer \, Dawson's Creek \, Empire Records \, and the platinum-selling F
 riends soundtrack — and their fans never left. “It's like a reunion of
  sorts\,” says Dean Dinning. “It's almost like having family in the au
 dience every night.”\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.me
 etboston.com/event/toad-the-wet-sprocket/90807/
LOCATION:The Wilbur\, 246 Tremont Street\, Boston\, MA\, 02116
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/toad-the-wet-sprocket/90807/
END:VEVENT
