DESCRIPTION:Join Revolutionary Spaces\, the Adams Presidential Center\, an
 d GBH Forum Network on Thursday\, October 29 at for an engaging conversati
 on exploring the remarkable leadership and enduring contributions of John 
 and Abigail Adams and their relevance to America today. Renowned historian
 s and civic education leaders Dr. Colleen Shogan and Dr. Kurt Graham will 
 come together at the Old South Meeting House for an insightful discussion 
 of the Adams family’s leadership\, civic values\, and lasting impact on 
 our constitutional democracy. This program is free and open to the public 
 thanks to the generous support of the Lowell Institute. Doors will open at
  6:00 PM and the program will begin at 6:30 PM. The program is also availa
 ble virtually and priority registration is available to Revolutionary Spac
 es members. Following the program\, a recording will be available on Revol
 utionary Spaces’ GBH Forum Network page. LEARN MORE\n\nSources: Meet Bos
