UID:4a3fe81d07347f5d56e4f52ee44d88@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Slapstick Film Series: Sherlock Jr. and Cops This October and 
 November\, the Clark hosts a series of silent slapstick comedy films that 
 highlight quick wit\, precarious situations\, and hilarious mishaps. The s
 eries continues with Sherlock Jr. (1924)\, in which an aspiring detective 
 is framed for stealing his girlfriend’s father’s watch and must hunt d
 own the true thief. Consistently listed among the 100 greatest films of al
 l time\, Sherlock Jr. delights viewers with its whimsical spirit and profo
 undly modernist inventions. The innovations are both narrative and visual
 \, leading to a much-emulated dream sequence. (Run time: 45 minutes) The s
 howing is preceded by Buster Keaton’s short film\, Cops (1922). (Run tim
 e: 18 minutes) A talkback with Will Schmenner\, film scholar and head of p
 ublic programs\, follows the screenings . Free. No registration required.
 \n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.
 com/event/clark-art-institute-a-flim-3/
