SUMMARY:US Army Jazz Ambassadors - Free Concert
DTSTART:20261029T000000
DTEND:20261029T000000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:7f4501a8db6383b8886d6ca096989c@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The internationally acclaimed Jazz Ambassadors of Washington\,
  DC will continue their long tradition of presenting free public performan
 ces when they appear in Hyannis\, MA at Barnstable High School Performing 
 Arts Center on Thursday\, October 29th\, 2026 at 7:00PM. The Jazz Ambassad
 ors' concert in Hyannis is presented in partnership with Barnstable Public
  Schools Performing Arts Department and ArtsBarnstable | Hyannis HyArts Cu
 ltural District. The Jazz Ambassadors is the official touring big band of 
 the United States Army. Formed in 1969\, this 19-member ensemble has recei
 ved great acclaim at home and abroad performing America's greatest origina
 l art form\, jazz. Concerts by the Jazz Ambassadors are programmed to ente
 rtain all types of audiences. The band’s diverse repertoire includes big
  band swing\, bebop\, Latin\, contemporary jazz\, standards\, popular tune
 s\, traditional New Orleans jazz\, vocals\, and patriotic selections\, man
 y of which are written or arranged by members of the Jazz Ambassadors. The
  Jazz Ambassadors has appeared in all 50 states\, Canada\, Mexico\, Japan
 \, India\, and throughout Europe. Recent notable performances include conc
 erts at the Toronto Jazz Festival\, the Richmond Jazz Festival at Maymont
 \, the Kennedy Center Honors\, the Jazz Education Network Conference\, and
  an appearance on the Colbert Report. Gordon Goodwin\, Bobby Shew\, Ernie 
 Watts\, and the Dave Brubeck All-Star Quintet are just a few of the outsta
 nding jazz artists who have shared the stage with the Jazz Ambassadors. Th
 e band has been featured in joint concerts with Marvin Hamlisch and the Pi
 ttsburgh Symphony Orchestra\, the San Diego Symphony Orchestra\, the Seatt
 le Symphony Pops\, the Colorado Pops Orchestra\, and the New York Pops at 
 Carnegie Hall. The band’s rigorous touring schedule and reputation for e
 xcellence has earned it the title “America’s Big Band.” For addition
 al information about the Jazz Ambassadors' performance in Hyannis please c
 ontact The United States Army Field Band by phone at (301) 677-6586\, or v
 isit www.armyfieldband.com/calendar\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent pa
 ge: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/us-army-jazz-ambassadors-free-con
 cert/51980/
LOCATION:Barnstable High School Performing Arts Center\, Barnstable High S
 chool Performing Arts Center
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/us-army-jazz-ambassadors-free-con
 cert/51980/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Uzo Aduba: Owning Your Identity
DTSTART:20261029T000000
DTEND:20261029T000000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:6c6da0f9d14d83c8d55af89b0ceb64@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:“Growing up\, I never thought there was a seat for me\, so I
 've decided to build my own table. Come. Pull up a chair.” —Uzo Aduba 
 Three-time Emmy Award–winning actor\, best-selling author\, and advocate
  Uzo Aduba invites you to join in a powerful conversation about identity\,
  belonging\, resilience\, and courage. Aduba is best known for her standou
 t portrayal of Suzanne “Crazy Eyes” Warren in Orange Is the New Black
 \, for which she garnered two Emmy awards. She can most recently be seen s
 tarring in Netflix's The Residence\, and her previous credits include Netf
 lix’s Painkiller\, as well as the critically acclaimed FX series Mrs. Am
 erica\, in which Aduba won her third Emmy award for her portrayal of Repre
 sentative Shirley Chisolm. Drawing from her celebrated career on screen an
 d stage\, as well as her memoir\, The Road Is Good (Viking\, 2024)\, Aduba
  shares the deeply personal journey that shaped her voice\, purpose\, and 
 commitment to justice. With warmth\, humor\, and authenticity\, she explor
 es the transformative power of storytelling\, family\, and the enduring st
 rength of community while encouraging others to embrace their own unique p
 aths. Don't miss this inspiring evening that celebrates finding your place
 \, building a table with space for every voice\, and recognizing the power
  of our stories to create connection and change. LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS
 \n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/uzo
 -aduba%3a-owning-your-identity/93634/
LOCATION:Museum of Fine Arts\, Boston\, Museum of Fine Arts\, Boston 465 H
 untington Avenue\, Boston\, MA\, 02115
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/uzo-aduba%3a-owning-your-identity/936
 34/
END:VEVENT
