BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Turners Falls\, Talk
DTSTART:20261030T170000
DTEND:20261030T190000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:d422eccfdf185c060650317c2dcfb9@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The Remarkable Landscapes of the Montague Plains This illustra
 ted talk for adults explores the natural history of the Montague Plains th
 rough four complementary perspectives. Geologist Richard Little explains t
 he glacial lake Hitchcock origins of the Montague plain and why Turners Fa
 lls would not exist if not for this delta. Pat Conlin\, Habitat Biologist 
 at MassWildlife\, describes the agency’s long-term stewardship and resto
 ration of imperiled natural plant communities\, Caren Caljouw\, Prescribed
  Fire Manager at MassWildlife\, covers the benefits of prescribed fire\, a
 nd ecologist Mike Akresh\, PhD\, reviews findings from wildlife research c
 onducted there. Together they show how geology\, land management\, and eco
 logical research have shaped our understanding of one of New England’s m
 ost distinctive pine and oak barrens. There is time for questions followin
 g the presentations. Meet in the Great Hall.\n\nSources: Explore Western M
 ass\nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event/turners-falls-talk/
LOCATION:Great Falls Discovery Center\, 2 Avenue A\, Turners Falls\, MA\, 
 01376
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/turners-falls-talk/
END:VEVENT
