BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yin Yu Tang: A Chinese Home Tour
DTSTART:20261030T111500
DTEND:20261030T161500
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:bbb7f5a02dfbee86fce69c9b350f01@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside a 200-year-old Chinese home in Salem to experience
  Chinese art\, architecture and culture. For 200 years\, Yin Yu Tang stood
  in the rural village of Huang Cun in a mountainous region of southeastern
  China. Home to eight generations of the Huang family\, this house was dis
 mantled\, transported and re-erected at the Peabody Essex Museum in 2003 t
 hrough a partnership between PEM and the governmental authorities of Huizh
 ou\, in Anhui Province. Yin Yu Tang’s journey constitutes a landmark col
 laboration between Chinese and American architects\, artisans\, conservato
 rs\, engineers and museum experts. The home is presented as it was when th
 e family last lived there in 1982. Plan Your Visit Exercise care Please he
 lp us preserve the house for future generations by refraining from touchin
 g objects and the structure itself. Non-flash photography and videography 
 is permitted for personal use only. Tripods and selfie sticks are not allo
 wed. Please walk with care and watch out for uneven stonework and raised t
 hresholds. Store your belongings\, but keep your coat Yin Yu Tang is parti
 ally outdoors and may be cool in fall and winter. Strollers\, bags\, backp
 acks and umbrellas are not permitted in the house. Please leave them at th
 e coatroom or the cubbies by the Information desk. Our staff at the entran
 ce of the house can look after strollers. Pick up your audio guide in adva
 nce Please pick up your complimentary audio guide\, available in English a
 nd Mandarin\, at the Information desk 10 minutes before your visit. Please
  note: Plan to bring your own pair of headphones. Before your visit\, pres
 s #50 to listen to an introduction to the house. Once inside\, look for st
 one blocks with two-digit numbers. Press the number plus the play > button
  to hear the audio. Be prompt Please be at the doors to Yin Yu Tang five m
 inutes before your scheduled visit with your audio guide in hand. A staff 
 member will alert you shortly before the end of your time slot.\n\nSources
 : North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang
 -a-chinese-home-tour/2026-10-30/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, East India Square\, 161 Essex Street\, Sal
 em\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang-a-chinese-home-tour/2026-1
 0-30/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Navy-Notre Dame Game
DTSTART:20261031T000000
DTEND:20261031T000000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:3185b7ad86b296cbf6caef9ffd35d7@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the Navy-Notre Dame Game on October 31\, 2026. Don
 ’t miss your chance to witness this historic game when these two teams m
 eet for the first time in the 99-game series in New England. The 2026 inst
 allment of Navy-Notre Dame will mark the Fighting Irish’s first time pla
 ying at Gillette Stadium\, and the Midshipmen’s second appearance at the
  home of the New England Patriots and Revolution after competing there in 
 the 2023 Army-Navy Game presented by USAA. Navy will be the home team for 
 the 2026 iteration of the game\, while Notre Dame will be the visiting tea
 m. The history of the Navy-Notre Dame Game dates back to 1927\, when two o
 f the nation’s oldest football programs first met on the field. The seri
 es was the longest continuous intersectional rivalry in college football\,
  playing 93 consecutive years from 1927-2019\, before COVID-19 canceled th
 e 2020 game.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.c
 om/event/2026-navy-notre-dame-game/93118/
LOCATION:Gillette Stadium at Patriot Place\, One Patriot Place\, Foxboroug
 h\, MA\, 02035
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/2026-navy-notre-dame-game/93118/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Amelia Park\, Imagination Awakened
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:37fa1cf5b011169c495878112c053e@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:**There’s a magical moment just before darkness falls…** W
 hen the last golden rays of sunlight begin to disappear beyond the trees\,
  the sky turns to shades of violet and blue\, and something extraordinary 
 begins to happen… The familiar slowly becomes unfamiliar. The shadows st
 retch a little farther. The lights begin to shimmer. Wisps of fog dance al
 ong the pathways\, and what was once a quiet garden begins to awaken. **An
 d suddenly… you’re not just walking through a garden anymore.** You’
 re stepping into a world where imagination has no boundaries. Across **1.3
  acres of winding pathways and wonderfully different themed worlds**\, you
 ’ll discover towering figures\, mysterious creatures\, whimsical surpris
 es\, and extraordinary sights waiting around every corner. Some will make 
 you smile. Others will leave you wide-eyed. And a few might just make you 
 stop in your tracks\, look up\, and whisper… **”WOW.”** Around every
  bend\, another opportunity to capture a little magic. A photograph beside
  something larger than life. A child gazing upward in amazement. A family 
 laughing together beneath the glow of the lights. **Because sometimes\, th
 e most magical part of an experience isn’t what we create… it’s the 
 wonder we see reflected in the faces of those experiencing it.** This isn
 ’t about jump scares or frightening anyone. It’s about atmosphere\, di
 scovery\, creativity\, and the beautiful feeling of letting your imaginati
 on run free. For the young\, the young at heart\, and anyone who still bel
 ieves that a little magic can exist in the world… **The garden is waitin
 g for you.** **YOUR INVITATION TO WONDER** Imagination Awakened — A Wick
 edly Wonderful Westfield Experience Presented by Imagination Preservation 
 Society and Holiday Preservation Society Amelia Park Memorial Garden\, 21 
 South Broad Street\, Westfield\, MA Sensory Thursdays: Oct 15\, 22\, 29 | 
 5–9 PM. Illuminated\, stationary and silent animatronics\; lighting\, fo
 g\, bubbles and photo opportunities remain. Quieter\, not sensory-free. Fu
 ll experience: Fridays Oct 16\, 23\, 30 | 5–9 PM\; Saturdays Oct 17\, 24
 \, 31 and Sundays Oct 18\, 25 | noon–9 PM. Sound and movement active\; n
 o jump scares. Last admission 9 PM\; gates close 10 PM. Admission: Adults 
 $20\, seniors $15\, ages 4–18 $10\, ages 3 and under FREE\; ticketing fe
 es may apply. General admission tickets valid once on any scheduled date. 
 Advance tickets (help shorten gate lines) General admission tickets are va
 lid for one visit on any scheduled event day. Purchasing ahead helps keep 
 the lines shorter and the magic flowing!\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass
 \nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event/amelia-park-imagination
 -awakened/2026-10-31/
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/amelia-park-imagination-awakened/
 2026-10-31/
END:VEVENT
