 -wide trick-or-treat experience. Then\, from 8 PM onward\, the fun shifts 
 to adults-only with hidden “Trick” and “Treat” cards placed throug
 hout Kings. Tricks might include bowling a frame with a non-dominant hand
 \, while treats can include free appetizers and other prizes. Costumes are
  encouraged for both experiences. Guests can also channel their spooky vib
 es with the Boo’s Bag ($13)\, an IV-style drink bag filled with Ghost Te
 quila\, Blood Orange\, Fresh Lemon & Lime\, Triple Sec\, available from Oc
 t. 12 - 31.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.co
