BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Norman Rockwell Museum\, Walking Tours
DTSTART:20261031T130000
DTEND:20261031T140000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:aac163a4e4f90c9437e70209f3c400@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Take a guided walking tour of downtown Stockbridge and discove
 r how the town and its inhabitants both inspired Norman Rockwell and appea
 red in some of his most iconic works of art. Explore the history of this 1
 734 village–including its Mohican origins. Stops will include Norman Roc
 kwell’s home on South Street\, his first studio on Main Street\, the Old
  Corner House (site of the original Norman Rockwell Museum)\, Chief John K
 onkapot’s property\, the Red Lion Inn\, the former site of Alice’s Res
 taurant\, and more! Limited capacity- advance reservations required. Meet 
 in front of The Old Corner House\, 48 Main Street\; public on street parki
 ng\, or designated spaces at Town Hall. Tour route is mostly flat\, and on
  sidewalks. Group size minimum of 10\, maximum of 15. Buy Tickets $20\; se
 parate from Museum Admission These tours do not take place at the Museum. 
 Tour groups will meet on Main Street. Transportation to Main Street from t
 he Museum is not provided.\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: h
 ttps://explorewesternmass.com/event/norman-rockwell-museum-walking-tours-2
 /2026-10-31/
LOCATION:Norman Rockwell Museum\, 9 Route 183 (Glendale Ave)\, Stockbridge
 \, MA\, 01262
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/norman-rockwell-museum-walking-to
 urs-2/2026-10-31/
END:VEVENT
