BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Make a Mosaic Workshop
DTSTART:20261104T000000
DTEND:20261219T000000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:8bef4f33e1ddfa6777d9a0bd0bcbdd@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Curious about mosaic art but not sure where to begin? Join us 
 for this beginner-friendly workshop and learn the fundamentals of mosaic m
 aking. Guided by an experienced instructor\, you'll explore mosaic design 
 and layout\, glass and tile cutting techniques\, and the grouting process.
  Whether you arrive with a specific idea in mind or are looking for inspir
 ation\, your instructor will help bring your creative vision to life. We'l
 l also provide plenty of design ideas to get you started. Your registratio
 n includes all materials needed to complete your project\, as well as your
  choice of several base options to work on such as a mirror\, picture fram
 e\, trivet\, or coaster set. We look forward to creating with you! 100% of
  proceeds from online sales and class registrations directly support SGM's
  educational programs\, community outreach\, and the preservation of our c
 ollections.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodc
 hamber.org/event/make-a-mosaic-workshop/52623/
LOCATION:Sandwich Glass Museum\, 129 Main St\, Sandwich\, MA\, 02563
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/make-a-mosaic-workshop/52623/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monthly International Book Club - Mona's Eyes
DTSTART:20261104T000000
DTEND:20261104T000000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:95fd3343d94ea3892473fc8ecf6c74@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:International Book Group – Mona’s Eyes by Thomas Schlesser
  The International Book Group at West Falmouth Library is a volunteer-led 
 group that meets on the first Wednesday of each month 3:45-5 p.m. Selectio
 ns have either foreign settings or foreign authors\, usually both. New mem
 bers are always welcome! Annual registration is requested to receive impor
 tant communications about schedule or location changes\; register below. M
 eetings are both in-person and on Zoom. The Wednesday\, November 4 meeting
  will discuss Mona’s Eyes by Thomas Schlesser. Ten-year-old Mona and her
  beloved grandfather have only fifty-two Wednesdays to visit fifty-two wor
 ks of art and commit to memory “all that is beautiful in the world” be
 fore Mona loses her sight forever. “No surprise that the novel’s autho
 r is a professor of art history at the École Polytechnique in Paris\; his
  characters channel his dazzling command of the greats.”—Hyperallergic
  “A French art historian’s English-language fiction debut combines the
  story of a loving relationship between a grandfather and granddaughter wi
 th an enlightening discussion of art… Come for the novel\, stay for the 
 introductory art history course.”—Kirkus Reviews “[A] life-affirming
  narrative.”—Booklist Online Register Here\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chambe
 r\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/monthly-international-
 book-club-monas-eyes/52273/
LOCATION:West Falmouth Library\, 575 West Falmouth Highway\, West Falmouth
 \, MA\, 02574
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/monthly-international-book-club-m
 onas-eyes/52273/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents May Exhibitions at 65 Water Street
DTSTART:20261104T110000
DTEND:20261104T170000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:750804feaddf636425aebdb315d4cb@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) presents three new shows opening in the 
 month of May! Soft Structures is a group exhibition that explores fibers a
 nd fibrous material as process and metaphor. This exhibit features over 80
  artworks in a variety of media including drawing\, painting\, sculpture\,
  weaving\, embroidery\, quilting\, collage\, mixed media and more. This ex
 hibit is on view in the first-floor Sargent Gallery and second-floor Harts
 on Gallery. FOLIA is a collaborative exhibition featuring works by Amesbur
 y artists Amy Vander Els & Heather Karp. This exhibit explores the quiet b
 eauty and joyful rhythm of leaves and the symbolic meaning behind many tha
 t speaks of perseverance\, resilience and hope. Thirty-six artworks are di
 splayed amongst spring greenery in the first-floor Hills Gallery. Amy and 
 Heather will give a free artist talk on Thursday\, May 21st from 6:00-7:00
 pm\, concluding with Q&A. The 11th Annual Outdoor Sculpture Garden Exhibit
 ion debuted on May 1st\, and will remain on view year-round until April 20
 27. At nearly 3\,000 square feet\, the Range Lights Sculpture Garden resid
 es behind the historic NAA and is seen and visited by hundreds of people e
 very week. This year’s exhibition features 16 pieces by 10 local and reg
 ional artists. The participating artists include\; Jeffrey Briggs\, Lindle
 y Briggs\, Sarah Burns and Mike Platt\, Alexis Guieb-Alimbuyuguen\, Andrew
  Henschel\, Mae Kenny\, Evan Ralph\, Michael Updike and Raynor Warner. A r
 eception for FOLIA and Soft Structures will be held on Saturday\, May 2nd 
 from 4-6pm\, with the 11th Annual Sculpture Exhibit reception beginning at
  3:00pm\, including a Best in Show award at 3:30pm. The receptions are fre
 e and open to the public\, and visitors participating in the May 2nd Newbu
 ryport Artwalk are encouraged to stop by. New Hours: Wednesday through Sun
 day from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More inform
 ation\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. F
 ounded in 1948\, Newburyport Art\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit\, is dedicated t
 o promoting and exhibiting members’ work and to providing art education 
 and access to the visual arts for the entire community. The gallery and ev
 ents are free and open to the public.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent p
 age: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibiti
 ons-at-65-water-street/2026-11-04/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibitio
 ns-at-65-water-street/2026-11-04/
END:VEVENT
