BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Eric Carle Museum\, The Carle After Dark
DTSTART:20261105T160000
DTEND:20261105T190000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:58cb81366fe294ccb6ffb3a2219526@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Discover The Carle in a whole new light! Join us on the first 
 Thursday of each month\, when the Museum transforms into a playground of w
 onder—celebrating storytelling\, color\, and art. Join us after hours an
 d bring your friends. Each month unveils a new adventure: peering into the
  cosmos\, gathering for storytelling\, singing into the stars\, and celebr
 ating picture books. Enjoy art making\, lively performances and activities
 \, and whimsical themed drinks as we gather at a place where community\, i
 magination\, and story come alive. We can’t wait to see you! All Museum 
 spaces are open during this time. See a list of events and activities belo
 w. Pay as You Wish! Become a member to enjoy free admission and year-round
  discounts in The Carle Bookshop . November 5— “Moo” ment How can a 
 still picture feel full of movement? Inspired by our exhibition Under the 
 Cork Tree: The Story of Ferdinand as part of The Carle After Dark series\,
  “Moo”ment invites families to explore the many ways artists use line
 \, gesture\, shape\, and expression to capture action and stillness. Throu
 ghout the Museum\, movement experiences will encourage guests to stretch\,
  pose\, freeze\, sway\, and observe how bodies communicate without words. 
 Families can experiment with drawing challenges\, respond to movement thro
 ugh mark-making\, and explore how a single line can suggest speed\, energy
 \, emotion\, or calm. In the Art Studio\, artists of all ages can create w
 ork inspired by motion\, using open-ended materials to capture a leap\, a 
 swirl\, a pause\, or a moment of quiet. Story Times at 4:30\, 5:30\, and 6
 :30 p.m. will feature books filled with movement\, rhythm\, and expressive
  characters. Come move\, make\, observe\, and pause as we discover how art
 ists bring energy to the page\, and how even the smallest “moo”ment ca
 n tell a story. Live music is sponsored by Northampton Jazz Fest and produ
 ced by Nate Gowen. December 3— Spinning Stories How can a still picture 
 feel full of movement? Inspired by our exhibition Under the Cork Tree: The
  Story of Ferdinand as part of The Carle After Dark series\, “Moo”ment
  invites families to explore the many ways artists use line\, gesture\, sh
 ape\, and expression to capture action and stillness. Throughout the Museu
 m\, movement experiences will encourage guests to stretch\, pose\, freeze
 \, sway\, and observe how bodies communicate without words. Families can e
 xperiment with drawing challenges\, respond to movement through mark-makin
 g\, and explore how a single line can suggest speed\, energy\, emotion\, o
 r calm. In the Art Studio\, artists of all ages can create work inspired b
 y motion\, using open-ended materials to capture a leap\, a swirl\, a paus
 e\, or a moment of quiet. Story Times at 4:30\, 5:30\, and 6:30 p.m. will 
 feature books filled with movement\, rhythm\, and expressive characters. C
 ome move\, make\, observe\, and pause as we discover how artists bring ene
 rgy to the page\, and how even the smallest “moo”ment can tell a story
 . Live music is sponsored by Northampton Jazz Fest and produced by Nate Go
 wen. January 7—Color Quest 2: The Shape of Things Through playful design
  challenges and open-ended artmaking\, transform simple shapes into imagin
 ative creations. February 4—Stories We Carry Bring a meaningful object
 —or discover one through a creative prompt—and reflect on the moments 
 that make everyday things extraordinary. March 4—Story Slam Gather for a
 n evening of shared experiences\, creative prompts\, and joyful conversati
 on that celebrates the ways stories connect us. Apr 1—Color Quest 3: Ins
 pired Create your own artistic response as you explore the connections bet
 ween Eric Carle and the modern artists who inspired his work. May 6—Gift
 s We Share Celebrate the traditions and memories we pass along through col
 laborative artmaking and storytelling inspired by the gifts that shape our
  lives. June 3—If I Were the Curator Step into the role of a museum cura
 tor as you design your own exhibition inspired by The Carle’s permanent 
 collection.\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://explorew
 esternmass.com/event/the-eric-carle-museum-the-carle-after-dark-2/2026-11-
 05/
LOCATION:The Eric Carle Museum of Picture Book Art\, 125 W Bay Road\, Amhe
 rst\, MA\, 01002
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/the-eric-carle-museum-the-carle-a
 fter-dark-2/2026-11-05/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:UMass Fine Arts Center\, Ruby Ibarra
DTSTART:20261105T193000
DTEND:20261105T210000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:7c94746614b51c737188508a62bb99@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Odds are\, you don’t need us to tell you how amazing Ruby Ib
 arra is. Maybe you’ve been with her from the moment she emerged onto the
  national scene back in 2011. Or you jumped on with her debut record Circa
 91 (2017\, Beatrock Music). Heard her stuff in a video game or a TV commer
 cial somewhere along the way. Caught her set at the Green River Festival i
 n June. Or\, like a lot of us\, watched her 2025 championship Tiny Desk co
 ncert over and over. It only ever takes one experience. You stumble into s
 o much as half a song and you’re hooked. On the other hand\, you might n
 eed us to advise you not to sleep on scoring tickets to this show. Yeah\, 
 it’s general admission\, and where you end up in the house will have mor
 e to do with when you arrive than when you buy. But consider these factors
 : This artist has hit a tipping point\; her popularity is growing exponent
 ially. And\, again\, she’s working these days with fellow Filipino Ameri
 can June Millington. You know Millington as a member of the pioneering all
 -women rock band Fanny\, a group cited as a major influence by acts from t
 he Runaways and the Bangles to Sleater Kinney and … well\, Ruby Ibarra. 
 You may or may not be aware that Millington is the co-founder and artistic
  director of Goshen’s Institute for the Musical Arts. She’s been part 
 of the western Massachusetts community for twenty-five years now. She has 
 friends. This show is going to melt Bowker Auditorium. And you’re going 
 to want to be there to see it. Total price starts at: $35.00. Total price 
 for youth 17 and under and Five College students starts at: $20.00. TICKET
 S\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass
 .com/event/umass-fine-arts-center-ruby-ibarra/
LOCATION:UMass Amherst\, 300 Massachusetts Ave\, Amherst\, MA\, 01003
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/umass-fine-arts-center-ruby-ibarr
 a/
END:VEVENT
