DTEND:20261107T150000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:d1703e03358cedaec253c520ad58ff@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The Clark presents a concert inspired by the newly acquired gr
 oup of portrait sculptures by Jean-Pierre Dantan\, part of the Aso O. Tavi
 tian Collection. Pianist David Kaplan\, acclaimed for his interpretations 
 of Robert Schumann\, curates a recital exploring musical caricature. Kapla
 n juxtaposes Schumann’s musical portraits of Frédéric Chopin\, Clara W
 ieck\, and others with music by several of Dantan’s subjects—Johann St
 rauss\, Sigismond Thalberg\, and Franz Liszt. Renowned music historian Jan
  Swafford introduces the program\, placing these works in the dynamic cont
 ext of 19th-century Romanticism. Tickets $15 ($12.75 members\, $12 college
  students\, $10 children 17 and under) . Buy Tickets\n\nSources: Explore W
 estern Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event/clark-art-in
 stitute-concert-4/
