DTEND:20261108T143000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:f465b1e38bf6946c67325bcf5a45de@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join local author and librarian Mk Smith Despres for a storyti
 me featuring their latest books in the First Friends board book series: Bo
 dies and Feelings! In First Friends: Bodies \, it’s time to move our bod
 ies! Can you raise your shoulders up and down? How about scrunching your f
 ace and spinning around? Let’s dance and shake our wiggles out before se
 ttling down on the rug for circle time. In First Friends: Feelings \, it
 ’s time for lunch! Some friends are feeling cranky\, frustrated\, or dow
 nright hangry. But caring friends and teachers help everyone deal with the
 ir big feelings. A book signing will follow the program. Can’t make it? 
 You may reserve signed books . Who You’ll Meet Mk Smith Despres Mk Smith
  Despres is the Youth Services Librarian at the Meekins Library in William
 sburg\, MA . In addition to the First Friends series\, they are the author
  of There’s That Sun Again and Night Song \, one of Bank Street’s Best
  Children’s Books of the Year. Author website\n\nSources: Explore Wester
 n Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event/the-eric-carle-mu
 seum-special-storytime/
LOCATION:The Eric Carle Museum of Picture Book Art\, 125 W Bay Road\, Amhe
 rst\, MA\, 01002
