DESCRIPTION:The Boutelle-Day Poetry Center presents Ama Codjoe / 2026 Crom
 well Day Poet Weinstein Auditorium\, Wright Hall\, Smith College The Boute
 lle-Day Poetry Center presents Poet Ama Codjoe on Cromwell Day. Codjoe wil
 l read from her most recent collection Bluest Nude. Cromwell Day is a Smit
 h tradition since 1989. The day honors Otelia Cromwell\, class of 1900\, a
 nd Smith’s first African American graduate\, with dedicated time for ref
 lection and education on diversity\, racism\, and inclusion.\n\nSources: E
 xplore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event/smit
 h-college-museum-of-art-author-talk/
LOCATION:Smith College Museum of Art\, 20 Elm Street at Bedford Terrace\, 
 Northampton\, MA\, 01063
