SUMMARY:Springfield\, Veterans Day Parade
DTSTART:20261111T110000
DTEND:20261111T120000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:3d6c606e2e6559d98eb11e84117904@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Mayor Sarno and other officials will hold a Veterans Day Parad
 e kicking off from Springfield Technical Community College at 11 a.m. and 
 finishing on the steps of City Hall with a ceremony and wreath laying at t
 he city’s Veterans Monument. People are encouraged to come out and cheer
  on the veterans! Rain or shine! Memorial Day: This federal holiday is cel
 ebrated the last Monday in May\, Memorial Day is the holiday set aside to 
 pay tribute to those who died serving in the military. Three years after t
 he Civil War ended\, on May 5\, 1868\, the head of an organization of Unio
 n veterans — the Grand Army of the Republic (GAR) — established Decora
 tion Day as a time for the nation to decorate the graves of the war dead w
 ith flowers. Maj. Gen. John A. Logan declared that Decoration Day should b
 e observed on May 30. It is believed that date was chosen because flowers 
 would be in bloom all over the country. The passage of the National Holida
 y Act of 1971 by Congress made it an official holiday. Veterans Day: This 
 federal holiday falls on November 11 and is designated as a day to honor a
 ll who have served in the military. Veterans Day began as Armistice Day to
  honor the end of World War I\, which officially took place on November 11
 \, 1918. Nov. 11 recognizes the month\, day and time the guns fell silent 
 on the Western Front during World War I. The carnage left millions dead\, 
 destroyed cities\, scorched countrysides and caused deep-seated resentment
 s that led to World War II. In 1954\, after having been through both World
  War II and the Korean War\, the 83rd U.S. Congress — at the urging of t
 he veterans service organizations — amended the Act of 1938 by striking 
 out the word “Armistice” and inserting the word “Veterans.” With t
 he approval of this legislation on June 1\, 1954\, November 11 became a da
 y to honor American veterans of all wars.\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass
 \nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event/springfield-veterans-da
 y-parade/
LOCATION:Downtown Springfield\, Main Street\, Springfield\, MA\, 01103
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/springfield-veterans-day-parade/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Eric Carle Museum\, Special Storytime
DTSTART:20261111T110000
DTEND:20261111T113000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:4bbec91001a22316cd996f528de4b5@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Winter has come to the Green Wood\, and Hector Fox and his fri
 ends are busy preparing for a festive celebration. But when howling winds 
 and wild snows arrive\, the friends get lost in the storm. Will they find 
 their way home? Will all of their party plans go to waste? In their newest
 \, snowiest adventure\, Hector Fox and his woodland crew must rely on each
  other and their courage more than ever as they discover that friendship i
 s one of the greatest gifts of all. Join author/illustrator Astrid Sheckel
 s as she reads her latest picture book\, the long-awaited Hector Fox and t
 he Snowy Surprise \, answers questions\, and does a drawing demonstration.
  A book signing will follow the program. Can’t make it? You may reserve 
 signed books . Who You’ll Meet Astrid Sheckels Astrid Sheckels\, a nativ
 e of western Massachusetts\, has always enjoyed stories involving imaginar
 y animals\, so she feels right at home bringing an assortment of well-dres
 sed animals to life in her detailed watercolor illustrations. Her award-wi
 nning books include the Hector Fox and Friends series\, the Sea Dog series
 \, and Flora and the Jazzers . She describes her art as a mix of classic r
 ealism and whimsy. Find her on social media @astridsheckelsart. Artist web
 site\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewesternm
 ass.com/event/the-eric-carle-museum-special-storytime-7/
LOCATION:The Eric Carle Museum of Picture Book Art\, 125 W Bay Road\, Amhe
 rst\, MA\, 01002
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/the-eric-carle-museum-special-sto
 rytime-7/
END:VEVENT
