BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artful Conversations: John Sloan’s “Scavenger Rocks”
DTSTART:20261112T123000
DTEND:20261112T133000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:c9493e475981d6ed8557ab6c9840dc@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join Us Mid-Day for Artful Conversations Take a midday pause a
 nd experience one work of art in depth. Artful Conversations are informal
 \, docent-led gallery experiences that invite visitors to slow down\, look
  closely\, and engage in thoughtful conversation. Each session features a 
 work of art or object that is new to view—whether a recent acquisition o
 r a work newly installed in the galleries. The program begins in the Educa
 tion Room at our Downtown Campus with a brief introduction and visual cont
 ext before moving into the galleries for an extended exploration of the fe
 atured work. Guided by observation\, curiosity\, and conversation\, partic
 ipants are encouraged to share ideas\, consider different perspectives\, a
 nd discover new connections together. This week for Artful Conversations T
 he program will offer an in‑depth look at John Sloan’s Scavenger Rocks
 \, a recent acquisition that deepens our understanding of the artist’s l
 ong-standing ties to East Gloucester. The presentation begins with a brief
  overview of Sloan’s stays at the Red Cottage from 1914 to 1918\, a form
 ative period that shaped many of his most compelling Cape Ann paintings. F
 rom there\, the talk turns to the granite outcropping near Niles Beach\, d
 rawing on contemporary photographic documentation to illuminate the site
 ’s distinctive forms and its role in Sloan’s artistic process\, offeri
 ng a vivid\, tangible link between the artwork and the landscape that insp
 ired it. Dan Duffy and his wife Helene have been Innkeepers at the Beech T
 ree B&B in Rockport for 16 years. In this capacity\, he takes pride in ser
 ving as an ambassador of goodwill for travelers from around the world. He 
 is passionate about showcasing our region’s rich history\, geographical 
 uniqueness\, and artistic treasurers. As a Cape Ann Museum docent\, Dan us
 es his experience connecting with visitors while deepening his own knowled
 ge of the Museum and of the region’s vibrant social and cultural history
 .\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event
 /artful-conversations-john-sloans-scavenger-rocks/2026-11-12/
LOCATION:Cape Ann Museum\, 27 Pleasant Street\, Gloucester\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/artful-conversations-john-sloans-scave
 nger-rocks/2026-11-12/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Clark Art Institute\, a Flim
DTSTART:20261112T173000
DTEND:20261112T183000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:010fd62cc5fe87b39ed71df407bbe4@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:A hybrid narrative and documentary film\, The Tuba Thieves (20
 24) is a sonic portrait of Los Angeles. From 2011 to 2013\, tubas were sto
 len from Los Angeles high schools. This is not a story about thieves or mi
 ssing tubas. Instead\, it asks what it means to listen. The screening will
  be followed by a Q&A with Alison O’Daniel\, the film’s director\, and
  Will Schmenner\, film scholar and head of public programs. A 5 pm recepti
 on in the Manton Research Center reading room precedes the event . Live AS
 L interpretation will be provided. Free. Advance registration encouraged. 
 Accessible seats available. Call 413 458 0570 with any questions. Register
 \n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.
 com/event/clark-art-institute-a-flim-5/
LOCATION:Clark Art Institute\, 225 South Street\, Williamstown\, MA\, 0126
 7
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/clark-art-institute-a-flim-5/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Daily Guided & Self-Guided Tour of Hammond Castle Museum
DTSTART:20261112T090000
DTEND:20261112T153000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:57d7328aec01d7c0a8bfeceda5f766@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside the breathtaking home of one of the most prolific 
 inventors of the 20th century\, John Hays Hammond\, Jr. Hammond Castle Mus
 eum is a dynamic STEAM museum\,*blending its historical significance as bo
 th **a historic house museum and a lapidarium. Inside\, you’ll not only 
 discover ancient\, medieval\, and Renaissance architectural elements and a
 rtifacts—including stone archways\, sarcophagi\, grave markers\, and an 
 extraordinary collection of stone and marble works—but you’ll also fin
 d a vibrant museum offering fresh educational and cultural arts programmin
 g. Visitors can explore items from the archival collection that have not b
 een publicly seen in generations\, along with newly curated content and th
 e most up-to-date information on the provenance of many pieces in our coll
 ection. New this season\, the Museum features four temporary exhibits that
  explore John Hays Hammond Jr. as both an individual and a scientific inno
 vator. In the Natalie Hays Hammond Temporary Exhibit Room\, Curatorial Dir
 ector John Leysath presents Spinning Platters with Hammond: Inside the Wor
 ld of Vinyl Records\, on display from April 29th through August 31st. Begi
 nning September 10th and running through the end of the 2025 season on Jan
 uary 4th\, Leysath will showcase” Hammond in Italy: The Love Affair Betw
 een the Hammonds & Italian Culture.”Additionally\, the Inventions Exhibi
 t Room will highlight Hammond’s groundbreaking Videotape Technology duri
 ng the spring and summer months\, followed by Hammond’s ahead-of-their-t
 ime Advertising Signs in the fall and early winter. Listed on the National
  Register of Historic Places\, and a repeated Reader’s Choice Best of No
 rth Shore winner by Northshore Magazine and a Trip Advisor Traveler’s Ch
 oice award recipient for the last three consecutive years\,** you can trus
 t that your visit will be an unforgettable experience. New This Season: Ne
 w Daily Hours and Flexible Arrival Times for Self-Guided Tours Open daily 
 from 9:00 am to 3:30 pm\, with the last entrance at 2:45 pm. The Museum\, 
 Museum Shop\, and grounds close at 3:30 pm. Experience Hammond Castle Muse
 um at your own pace with our new flexible arrival times for self-guided to
 urs. Your ticket grants you entry anytime within designated periods\, ensu
 ring you can arrive stress-free and enjoy your visit to the fullest. Morni
 ng Session: 9:00 am – 11:45 am / Afternoon Session: 11:45 am – 2:30 pm
  Self-guided tours allow you to explore at your own pace. We recommend pla
 nning for at least 60 minutes to experience the Museum’s fascinating gal
 leries\, grounds\, and temporary exhibits. **Accessibility Note: Please be
  aware that at nearly a century old\, the Hammond Castle Museum is not han
 dicapped accessible due to many difficult and winding stairs on the campus
  and within the Museum\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://no
 rthofboston.org/event/daily-guided-self-guided-tour-of-hammond-castle-muse
 um/2026-11-12/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/daily-guided-self-guided-tour-of-hammo
 nd-castle-museum/2026-11-12/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eastern States Exposition\, Equine Affaire
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261112
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:720e9efe77f5a034fc4a7337486676@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Great Horses and Great People. So Much to Do . . . and Four Da
 ys to Do It In! Equine Affaire is all about opportunities! Learn from and 
 mingle with many of the foremost trainers\, coaches\, competitors\, judges
 \, and experts in the horse industry. Take a break from online shopping to
  see\, touch\, try on\, and experience a wealth of equine and equestrian p
 roducts in the largest horse-related trade shows in the nation. Meet and a
 ppreciate dozens of breeds of horses from around the world. Buy a horse—
 or sell one. Discover the right stallion for your mare or the ideal boardi
 ng\, training\, or breeding facility for you and your horse. Experience th
 e excitement of the Versatile Horse & Rider Competition (Equine Affaire’
 s ultimate test of horsemanship) and the drama of the Fantasia (Equine Aff
 aire’s signature musical celebration of the horse.) Interface with all f
 acets of the horse industry while sharing your passion for horses with fri
 ends\, family\, and fellow horse people. We invite you to take the opportu
 nity to immerse yourself in “all things equine” for four incredible da
 ys in November. EXPERIENCE the FANTASIA: Equine Affaire’s magical and mu
 sical celebration of the horse\, the Fantasia\, will take place at 7:30pm 
 on Thursday\, Friday\, and Saturday in the coliseum. The Fantasia will tak
 e you on a journey with spectacular performances by some of the foremost e
 quine and equestrian entertainers in the country ranging from a taste of t
 he wild west to the elegance and grace of Spanish garrocha\, daring acroba
 tics\, mesmerizing horses at liberty\, precision drill teams\, comedy\, an
 d much more. Clinics\, Seminars & Demonstrations: Enjoy an amazing program
  of more than 150 sessions including clinics on a wide variety of equestri
 an disciplines in three arenas presented by leading coaches\, competitors
 \, and trainers. Soak up a wealth of advice from industry experts on sessi
 ons covering the gamut of horse training\, horse management\, and equestri
 an subjects at the Demo Ring and the Seminar Stage. Whether you ride Engli
 sh or western\, prefer the show arena or the trail\, you’ll find a clini
 c at Equine Affaire to fit your discipline and riding interests. Through E
 quine Affaire’s Ride With The Best program you can receive individual in
 struction from – or have your horse trained by – one of the nations’
  foremost horsemen and women for a very affordable clinic fee that include
 s stabling and event admission. Breed and Horse & Farm Exhibits: Learn abo
 ut dozens of horse breeds from North America\, Europe\, and beyond at the 
 Breed Pavilion and the Horse & Farm Exhibits. Representatives of horse\, p
 ony\, and color associations and registries will be on hand to answer your
  questions about their breeds and registries. Equines from ponies to draft
 s and from stock horses to sport horses will be on exhibit\, with many hos
 ting breed demonstrations. The Horse & Farm Exhibits will also showcase a 
 vast number of stallions\, breeding farms\, training facilities\, and hors
 e facilities. SHOP: one of North America’s largest equine-related trade 
 shows with 350+ exhibitors. From jewelry to tack to equestrian apparel\, t
 railers\, farm equipment\, and so much more\, we know you’ll find exactl
 y what you’re looking for. Visit www.equineaffaire.com for continuously-
 updated information about the event as well as tips for making the most of
  your trip to the show. Grab some of your favorite Big E bites during Equi
 ne Affaire including Billie’s Baked Potato\, Butcher Boys\, Calabrese Ma
 rket\, Soulfully Vegan\, and so many more! Open Thurs. – Sat. 9am-7pm an
 d Sun.\, 9am-5pm Better Living Center\, Young & Stroh Buildings\, Mallary 
 Complex\, Coliseum Purchase your tickets online at equineaffaire.com or by
  calling our office directly at 740-845-0085. Either way\, you’ll receiv
 e your tickets to Equine Affaire (and Fantasia!) digitally \, straight to 
 your email inbox. From there\, you can save them to your phone or print th
 em off.\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://exploreweste
 rnmass.com/event/eastern-states-exposition-presents-equine-affaire/
LOCATION:Eastern States Exposition\, 1305 Memorial Avenue\, West Springfie
 ld\, MA\, 01089
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/eastern-states-exposition-present
 s-equine-affaire/
END:VEVENT
