BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ECOC Lecture: The Resplendent Quetzal
DTSTART:20261113T194500
DTEND:20261113T210000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:52b667682e08d4baa60c00eea6e561@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join ornithologist Alan Poole for an exploration into the life
  and history of the Resplendent Quetzal — a dazzling\, legendary bird of
  the highland forests of Central America. Author of the recent book Quetza
 ls: Icons of the Cloud Forest (2023)\, Poole will lead us through the nest
 ing and feeding ecology of this renowned bird\, its role in Mayan and Azte
 c religions\, and how Resplendents fit into the increasingly threatened ra
 in forests that sustain them. In addition\, we’ll take a look at what li
 es ahead for this (and other) quetzals — how conservation efforts are gi
 ving them a boost in some regions\, while in others the birds are struggli
 ng. This talk will touch on land use in Central America\, especially Costa
  Rica\, through a quetzal lens. No species does more to bring current land
  use trends in this region into focus. Understanding those trends is key t
 o maintaining the viability of highland tropical forests in the Americas\,
  and the quetzals that depend on them. A book signing will follow the prog
 ram.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/ev
 ent/ecoc-lecture-the-resplendent-quetzal/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, East India Square\, 161 Essex Street\, Sal
 em\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/ecoc-lecture-the-resplendent-quetzal/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Glass Etching Workshop
DTSTART:20261113T000000
DTEND:20261216T000000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:be9775aab63976b354aae5ad1e5c63@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Discover the art of glass etching in this hands-on creative wo
 rkshop! Guests will design and tape their own custom pattern onto a glass 
 piece of their choice—options may include a wine glass\, pint glass\, or
  small dish. Once your design is in place\, your instructor will carefully
  sandblast the piece\, revealing a beautifully etched version of your artw
 ork. This beginner-friendly experience covers the basics of glass etching 
 while giving you the freedom to create something uniquely yours. Whether y
 ou design a simple pattern\, monogram\, or decorative motif\, you’ll lea
 ve with a gorgeous\, functional piece that’s perfect for your kitchen or
  as a personalized gift. No prior experience is needed\; just bring your c
 reativity and enjoy the process of transforming everyday glass into a cust
 om work of art! Ticket covers one piece\; guests may add on an additional 
 piece day of for $25 if they wish.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent pag
 e: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/glass-etching-workshop/52621/
LOCATION:Sandwich Glass Museum\, 129 Main Street\, Sandwich\, MA\, 02563
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/glass-etching-workshop/52621/
END:VEVENT
