BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Norman Rockwell Museum\, Talk
DTSTART:20261114T160000
DTEND:20261114T170000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:77ebf67c747f62ac8e18dc482aeb4f@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Exploring Bill Watterson’s Calvin and Hobbes : Illustrated L
 ecture From 1985 to 1995\, Bill Watterson created one of the most celebrat
 ed and beloved newspaper comic strips of all time: Calvin and Hobbes . The
  strip featured the adventures (and misadventures) of 6-year-old Calvin an
 d his trusty companion\, Hobbes. Join exhibition curator\, Jenny Robb for 
 a lecture exploring Watterson’s masterful artistry and storytelling\, th
 e evolution of the strip\, and his place in the history of American newspa
 per comics. Robb will present exclusive recordings of Watterson discussing
  the strip and his process and will offer insights into Watterson’s insp
 irations\, including cartoonists George Herriman and Charles M. Schulz\, w
 hose work is also view. Jenny Robb is Head Curator of Comics and Cartoon A
 rt at the Billy Ireland Cartoon Library & Museum\, which houses the Bill W
 atterson Collection of more than 3\,000 original Calvin and Hobbes daily a
 nd Sunday comic strips. In collaboration with Watterson\, she curated the 
 exhibition “ Exploring Calvin and Hobbes ”\, which opens at the Norman
  Rockwell Museum on November 14th. Exploring Bill Watterson’s Calvin and
  Hobbes: Illustrated Lecture Buy Tickets $15* Limited seating\; reservatio
 ns required.\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://explore
 westernmass.com/event/norman-rockwell-museum-talk/
LOCATION:Norman Rockwell Museum\, 9 Route 183 (Glendale Ave)\, Stockbridge
 \, MA\, 01262
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/norman-rockwell-museum-talk/
END:VEVENT
