DTEND:20261114T120000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:e23bb213324bd972c333dfc5e1b059@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:From the ofrendas of Dia de los Muertos to butsudan in Japanes
 e Buddhist homes\, many different cultures create spaces for honoring ance
 stors. As the days grow shorter\, join us for a reflective art workshop th
 at reflects on those who came before us. Through simple mixed-media assemb
 lage\, participants will create a personal altar or remembrance piece that
  celebrates family\, chosen family\, mentors\, cultural heritage or loved 
 ones who have shaped their lives. No prior art experience is needed. All m
 aterials will be provided\, and participants are invited to bring copies o
 f photographs or small paper mementos they may wish to incorporate into th
 eir artwork. Studio Saturdays is a series of adult art making classes desi
 gned to inspire creativity and connection through multimedia arts explorat
 ion. Each class includes an arts activity that will inspire collaboration
 \, curiosity and creativity\, culminating in a completed individual artwor
 k and communal sharing.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://n
 orthofboston.org/event/remembrance-altars/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, East India Square\, 161 Essex Street\, Sal
 em\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/remembrance-altars/
END:VEVENT
