UID:d2ae9006f235f8a67ae1570777e360@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for a gallery preview of selected works schedul
 ed for Paul Schulenburg's solo exhibition at the St. Botolph Club in Bosto
 n starting in December. The works going to Boston may be previewed here ht
 tps://addisonart.com/schulenburg-stbotolphClub/ If there are any pieces yo
 u would particularly like to see before they go to Boston\, please let us 
 know and we will bring them into the gallery. The St. Botolph Club\, locat
 ed at 199 Commonwealth Avenue\, was founded in 1880. It promoted the new a
 rt of its time\, and sponsored John Singer Sargent's first one-man show in
  America in 1888. Works by Claude Monet were displayed in 1892\, 1895\, an
 d 1899. By 1900\, the Club had sponsored solo exhibitions of virtually eve
 ry important American Impressionist of the era including Childe Hassam\, T
 heodore Wendel\, John L. Breck\, Edmund Tarbell\, and Mary Cassatt. We hop
 e you can join us in celebrating this prestigious show.\n\nSources: Cape C
 od Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/schulenburg-p
 review-reception/52681/
LOCATION:Addison Art Gallery\, 43 South Orleans Road (Route 28)\, Orleans
 \, MA\, 02653
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/schulenburg-preview-reception/526
 81/
