BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Montague\, Benefit Concert
DTSTART:20261115T160000
DTEND:20261115T200000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:961d07e9a39b69c7f37a39a0bdf800@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:On Sunday\, November 15\, acclaimed cornetist\, composer\, and
  bandleader Taylor Ho Bynum brings his quintet to Montague Common Hall for
  an afternoon improvisation workshop and an evening concert\, with special
  guest the Montague Marching Band. Presented by Weathervane Community Arts
  as a benefit for the Montague Common Hall’s new Accessibility Plan\, th
 e day offers a rare chance to encounter one of creative music’s most inv
 entive voices up close\, in an intimate hometown setting. The day begins a
 t 4 PM with a workshop open to musicians of all skill levels\, who are inv
 ited to experience Bynum’s distinctive methods of “conduction” and i
 mprovisation. Those participants then take the stage as part of the evenin
 g concert — a participatory event that dissolves the line between perfor
 mer and audience. At 6:30 PM\, Bynum is joined by Noah Campbell (saxophone
 )\, Ziaire Trinidad Sherman (saxophone)\, Daniel Lin (cello)\, and Luther 
 Gray (drums) for a concert featuring the workshop participants and the Mon
 tague Marching Band — a beloved\, mixed-level\, multigenerational street
  band perhaps best known for its regular appearances at the Montague Cente
 r Halloween festivities. Bynum’s music draws on the full lineage of jazz
  and experimental composition — expressionistic\, unpredictable\, and de
 eply collaborative — shaped over two decades alongside the legendary Ant
 hony Braxton and more than twenty albums as a bandleader. Suggested donati
 on is $20 concert\, $20 workshop\, $30 for both\, with no one turned away 
 for lack of funds. All proceeds will benefit. the Montague Common Hall’s
  new Accessibility Plan\, which includes a new wheelchair ramp to make the
  historic hall welcoming to all. The events take place Sunday\, November 1
 5 at Montague Common Hall\, 34 Main St\, Montague\, MA. Tickets and detail
 s at www.weathervane-arts.org . Contact Jesse Bay at (510) 387-0765 or wea
 thervane.community.arts@gmail.com.\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent
  page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event/montague-benefit-concert/
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/montague-benefit-concert/
END:VEVENT
