BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:UNEARTHING JOY IN CRITICAL LITERACY DISCUSSIONS
DTSTART:20261119T000000
DTEND:20261119T000000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:0b93b18608cd91305911aca2b6f84c@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:In this free professional development seminar\, Peter Piazza\,
  Ph.D.\, will discuss strategies for critical literacy instruction\, as dr
 awn from Gholdy Muhammad’s “Unearthing Joy.” A key text in Stonehill
 ’s Justice & Anti-Discrimination in Education program\, “Unearthing Jo
 y” guides teachers through Muhammad’s framework for moving beyond our 
 narrow focus on rote learning and test-based measurement. This virtual sem
 inar will highlight key strategies for building students’ critical refle
 ction skills and\, indeed\, returning joy to learning. After discussing th
 e framework\, participants will look at an example lesson plan developed b
 y a Stonehill graduate student based on the “Unearthing Joy” model.\n
 \nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/ev
 ent/unearthing-joy-in-critical-literacy-discussions/52565/
LOCATION:Stonehill College Division of Graduate and Professional Studies\,
  320 Washington Street Stonehill College\, NORTH EASTON\, MA\, 02356
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/unearthing-joy-in-critical-litera
 cy-discussions/52565/
END:VEVENT
