BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:UMass Fine Arts Center\, ¡Guitarra! João Luiz Rezende Lopes
DTSTART:20261121T193000
DTEND:20261121T210000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:808b9364a3b088d5b115615d06ed58@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Best known as a member of the acclaimed Brasil Guitar Duo\, Jo
 ão Luiz Rezende Lopes is a two-time Latin Grammy-nominated guitarist\, ed
 ucator\, and composer. As a performer and composer\, he is equally at home
  with classical\, Brazilian\, and world music. His solo guitar\, chamber m
 usic\, and concerto repertoire covers all the main works in the guitar lit
 erature from Dowland to Berio\, and Brazilian rhythms from choro to baião
 . His arrangements and compositions have been recorded and played by Marin
 a Piccinini\, Fábio Zanon\, Quaternaglia\, Olson/De Cari Duo\, Danilo Bri
 to\, Paquito D’Rivera\, Clarice Assad\, Bridget Kibbey\, Jiji\, Sybarite
  5\, D-Composed\, Plínio Fernandes\, The Newman & Oltman guitar duo\, Aqu
 arelle Guitar Quartet\, David Leisner\, and the New York City Classical Gu
 itar Society. In 2024\, “Saravá\,” his composition for string quartet
  and guitar\, was honored with the prestigious São Paulo Art Critics Asso
 ciation’s award for Best New Work. Total price starts at: $35.00. Total 
 price for youth 17 and under and Five College students starts at: $25.00. 
 Tickets\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://exploreweste
 rnmass.com/event/umass-fine-arts-center-guitarra-joao-luiz-rezende-lopes/
LOCATION:UMass Amherst\, 300 Massachusetts Ave\, Amherst\, MA\, 01003
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/umass-fine-arts-center-guitarra-j
 oao-luiz-rezende-lopes/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Will Noonan at the Seacrest
DTSTART:20261121T000000
DTEND:20261121T000000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:811f402a0c57d65f665cf74fc86066@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Will Noonan will be joined by fellow comedians Will Smalley an
 d Ryan Ellington Will Noonan at the Sea Crest Will Noonan is one of Boston
 ’s most recognizable comedy stars\, known for his energetic storytelling
 \, sharp observations\, and unmistakable New England humor. Named “Bosto
 n’s Best Comedian” by The Improper Bostonian \, Will has appeared on F
 OX\, Hulu\, Gotham Comedy Live \, NPR’s This American Life \, and in the
  Netflix film The Sleepover . He is also familiar to audiences across New 
 England as “The Honda Guy” from his popular television and radio comme
 rcials. Joining him is feature comedian Will Smalley\, a standout voice in
  the Boston comedy scene known for his clever\, personal\, and refreshingl
 y original comedy. Boston comedian Ryan Ellington will host the evening an
 d keep the laughs and energy flowing from start to finish. Grab your ticke
 ts early for a night packed with some of New England’s funniest talent. 
 Doors open at 7pm & the show starts at 8 pm.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber
 \nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/will-noonan-at-the-seac
 rest/52682/
LOCATION:Flapjack Comedy Productions\, 350 Quaker Road\, North Falmouth\, 
 MA\, 02556
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/will-noonan-at-the-seacrest/52682
 /
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wistariahurst Museum\, Concert
DTSTART:20261121T180000
DTEND:20261121T190000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:bcbaf9087f0ccfa694a1fddf6a3d61@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join musician and storyteller Kemp Harris at Wistariahurst Mus
 eum for an evening of music and exploration. Join musician and storyteller
  Kemp Harris at Wistariahurst Museum for an evening of music and explorati
 on. Harris’ concert\, being held in the historic music room\, will take 
 visitors on a journey. His program will focus on family-friendly storytell
 ing. Kemp’s repertoire includes African folk tales\, original stories\, 
 and familiar stories in literature. Tickets to this concert are available 
 at a sliding scale price from $5-$20. Tickets are available online and can
  be purchased through Wistariahurst’s Eventbrite page. They can also be 
 purchased at the door. TICKETS About Kemp Harris: Kemp Harris is a singer 
 and songwriter\, a master weaver of American musical styles. He’s an act
 or\, activist\, author\, and storyteller\, and an award-winning educator w
 ho has taught young public school students for more than 40 years. “It
 ’s all about communication\,” Kemp says. “Everything I do.” Born i
 n segregated Edenton\, North Carolina\, and transplanted to Massachusetts
 \, where he bounced between homes\, Kemp learned to adapt to whatever worl
 d he found himself in – a talent that has come to define him as a person
  and an artist. He began writing songs at 14 and recording them in college
 \, using a pair of old cassette players to track parts\, and has been deli
 ghting audiences ever since with his earthy\, soulful creations. Learn mor
 e about Kemp Harris at https://www.kempharris.band/\n\nSources: Explore We
 stern Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event/wistariahurst
 -museum-concert/
LOCATION:Wistariahurst Museum\, 238 Cabot Street\, Holyoke\, MA\, 01040
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/wistariahurst-museum-concert/
END:VEVENT
