BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bright Nights at Forest Park
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261125
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:5f2c628c57d9a58f436b9eed356c4d@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Bright Nights at Forest Park will kick off its 32nd season on 
 Wednesday\, November 25\, with a special guest flipping the switch on all 
 750\,000 lights. In addition to the magical lighting display illuminating 
 the three-mile drive\, Santa’s Magical Forest will be welcoming visitors
  to enjoy\, snacks\, souvenirs\, and whirl on the carousel. Santa will be 
 greeting visitors at the entrance on opening night as well. Visitors will 
 be in awe as reindeer leap over cars. They will look to see which has the 
 red nose. The Blizzard Tunnel transports travelers to the North Pole Villa
 ge where elves toss toys into Santa’s sack\, while others tend to his sl
 eigh\, and more elves prefer to frolic and play. Santa can be seen flying 
 high above the historical Springfield Municipal Group. There are the Winte
 r Woods\, Winter Garden\, Garden of Peace\, and Jurassic World with a volc
 ano that shoots out snowflakes\, animated displays for the Springfield Thu
 nderbirds\, and MGM Springfield. There is a frog that leaps from his lily 
 pad and makes a splash. The 48-foot tall Giant Poinsettia Candles light th
 e way for a safe trip home. It is a magical holiday journey that has welco
 med more than 7 million visitors since 1995. BUY TICKETS November 25th –
  January 3rd Closed November 30th and December 1st Bright Nights 5K Road R
 ace Monday\, November 30th Rain Date: December 1st Bright Nights Roll Back
  Night Wednesday\, November 25\, 5pm to 9pm Admission Price $6 per car\, S
 ame as our opening year in 1995! Tickets must be purchased in advance. No 
 coupons will be accepted. $12 Tuesdays Tuesday\, December 8th & 15th Brigh
 t Nights Wagon Rides Climb aboard a wagon or the Cinderella Carriage and e
 njoy many of Bright Nights at Forest Park’s magical displays. The crisp 
 winter air and the clip-clop of the horses’ hooves make for a memorable 
 experience among the twinkling lights. The tour begins at the Bright Night
 s Gift Shop. Passengers are then carried away to enjoy the glimmer and glo
 w of Seuss Land\, the tranquility of the Garden of Peace\, and the jungle 
 of Jurassic World. Upon return to the gift shop\, they can purchase gifts 
 and souvenirs\, visit with Santa\, enjoy a tasty treat\, and bask in the g
 low of Bright Nights at Forest Park’s Grand Christmas Tree. The private 
 horse-drawn wagon for as many as 12 people is $300 and includes two compli
 mentary vehicle admission tickets for Bright Nights at Forest Park. The Ci
 nderella Carriage holds up to four people for $250 and includes one compli
 mentary vehicle admission ticket The wagon and carriage departs approximat
 ely every half hour starting at 5:30PM. The last departs at 8:30PM. Reserv
 ations Required Horse-Drawn Wagon Rides Thursday\, December 3 Thursday\, D
 ecember 10 Thursday\, December 17 Sunday\, December 27 Horse-Drawn Carriag
 e Rides Friday\, December 4 Friday\, December 11 Friday\, December 18 Sant
 a – Photos & Visits Bright Nights Welcomes Santa For Bright Nights at Fo
 rest Park from opening night to Christmas Eve. The big man in the red suit
  will be listening to holiday wish lists\, posing for photos\, his camera 
 or yours\, and spreading holiday cheer. Bright Nights Best of the Best Sin
 ce 1995\, Bright Nights has been a unique public/private collaboration bet
 ween the City of Springfield’s Department of Parks\, Buildings & Recreat
 ion Management and the Spirit of Springfield\, a private non-profit organi
 zation. Together they have welcomed more than 6 million visitors. It has b
 een calculated that if every bus that had visited were lined bumper to bum
 per\, they would go from Springfield to Cape Cod. The cars would go as far
  as California.\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://expl
 orewesternmass.com/event/bright-nights-at-forest-park/
LOCATION:Forest Park\, 300 Sumner Avenue\, Springfield\, MA\, 01108
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/bright-nights-at-forest-park/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents May Exhibitions at 65 Water Street
DTSTART:20261125T110000
DTEND:20261125T170000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:c2c98f9ff29e8f11f9287d5386bdd8@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) presents three new shows opening in the 
 month of May! Soft Structures is a group exhibition that explores fibers a
 nd fibrous material as process and metaphor. This exhibit features over 80
  artworks in a variety of media including drawing\, painting\, sculpture\,
  weaving\, embroidery\, quilting\, collage\, mixed media and more. This ex
 hibit is on view in the first-floor Sargent Gallery and second-floor Harts
 on Gallery. FOLIA is a collaborative exhibition featuring works by Amesbur
 y artists Amy Vander Els & Heather Karp. This exhibit explores the quiet b
 eauty and joyful rhythm of leaves and the symbolic meaning behind many tha
 t speaks of perseverance\, resilience and hope. Thirty-six artworks are di
 splayed amongst spring greenery in the first-floor Hills Gallery. Amy and 
 Heather will give a free artist talk on Thursday\, May 21st from 6:00-7:00
 pm\, concluding with Q&A. The 11th Annual Outdoor Sculpture Garden Exhibit
 ion debuted on May 1st\, and will remain on view year-round until April 20
 27. At nearly 3\,000 square feet\, the Range Lights Sculpture Garden resid
 es behind the historic NAA and is seen and visited by hundreds of people e
 very week. This year’s exhibition features 16 pieces by 10 local and reg
 ional artists. The participating artists include\; Jeffrey Briggs\, Lindle
 y Briggs\, Sarah Burns and Mike Platt\, Alexis Guieb-Alimbuyuguen\, Andrew
  Henschel\, Mae Kenny\, Evan Ralph\, Michael Updike and Raynor Warner. A r
 eception for FOLIA and Soft Structures will be held on Saturday\, May 2nd 
 from 4-6pm\, with the 11th Annual Sculpture Exhibit reception beginning at
  3:00pm\, including a Best in Show award at 3:30pm. The receptions are fre
 e and open to the public\, and visitors participating in the May 2nd Newbu
 ryport Artwalk are encouraged to stop by. New Hours: Wednesday through Sun
 day from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More inform
 ation\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. F
 ounded in 1948\, Newburyport Art\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit\, is dedicated t
 o promoting and exhibiting members’ work and to providing art education 
 and access to the visual arts for the entire community. The gallery and ev
 ents are free and open to the public.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent p
 age: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibiti
 ons-at-65-water-street/2026-11-25/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibitio
 ns-at-65-water-street/2026-11-25/
END:VEVENT
