BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bright Nights at Forest Park
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270104
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:676124c6f70ee7049705c48aaf28a5@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Travel through a dazzling wonderland of over 750\,00 lights at
  Bright Nights at Forest Park. This three-mile drive-thru spectacular feat
 ures festive scenes\, iconic characters\, and peaceful gardens\, all illum
 inated for a joyous holiday experience. In addition to the magical lightin
 g display illuminating the three-mile drive\, Santa’s Magical Forest wil
 l be welcoming visitors to enjoy\, snacks\, souvenirs\, and whirl on the c
 arousel. Visitors will be in awe as reindeer leap over cars. They will loo
 k to see which has the red nose. The Blizzard Tunnel transports travelers 
 to the North Pole Village where elves toss toys into Santa’s sack\, whil
 e others tend to his sleigh\, and more elves prefer to frolic and play. Sa
 nta can be seen flying high above the historical Springfield Municipal Gro
 up. There are the Winter Woods\, Winter Garden\, Garden of Peace\, and Jur
 assic World with a volcano that shoots out snowflakes\, animated displays 
 for the Springfield Thunderbirds\, and MGM Springfield. There is a frog th
 at leaps from his lily pad and makes a splash. The 48-foot tall Giant Poin
 settia Candles light the way for a safe trip home. It is a magical holiday
  journey that has welcomed more than 7 million visitors since 1995. BUY TI
 CKETS November 25th – January 3rd $12 Tuesdays Tuesday\, December 8th & 
 15th Bright Nights Wagon Rides Climb aboard a wagon or the Cinderella Carr
 iage and enjoy many of Bright Nights at Forest Park’s magical displays. 
 The crisp winter air and the clip-clop of the horses’ hooves make for a 
 memorable experience among the twinkling lights. The tour begins at the Br
 ight Nights Gift Shop. Passengers are then carried away to enjoy the glimm
 er and glow of Seuss Land\, the tranquility of the Garden of Peace\, and t
 he jungle of Jurassic World. Upon return to the gift shop\, they can purch
 ase gifts and souvenirs\, visit with Santa\, enjoy a tasty treat\, and bas
 k in the glow of Bright Nights at Forest Park’s Grand Christmas Tree. Th
 e private horse-drawn wagon for as many as 12 people is $300 and includes 
 two complimentary vehicle admission tickets for Bright Nights at Forest Pa
 rk. The Cinderella Carriage holds up to four people for $250 and includes 
 one complimentary vehicle admission ticket The wagon and carriage departs 
 approximately every half hour starting at 5:30PM. The last departs at 8:30
 PM. Reservations Required Horse-Drawn Wagon Rides Thursday\, December 3 Th
 ursday\, December 10 Thursday\, December 17 Sunday\, December 27 Horse-Dra
 wn Carriage Rides Friday\, December 4 Friday\, December 11 Friday\, Decemb
 er 18 Santa – Photos & Visits Bright Nights Welcomes Santa For Bright Ni
 ghts at Forest Park from opening night to Christmas Eve. The big man in th
 e red suit will be listening to holiday wish lists\, posing for photos\, h
 is camera or yours\, and spreading holiday cheer. Bright Nights Best of th
 e Best Since 1995\, Bright Nights has been a unique public/private collabo
 ration between the City of Springfield’s Department of Parks\, Buildings
  & Recreation Management and the Spirit of Springfield\, a private non-pro
 fit organization. Together they have welcomed more than 6 million visitors
 . It has been calculated that if every bus that had visited were lined bum
 per to bumper\, they would go from Springfield to Cape Cod. The cars would
  go as far as California.\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: ht
 tps://explorewesternmass.com/event/bright-nights-at-forest-park-2/
LOCATION:Forest Park\, 300 Sumner Avenue\, Springfield\, MA\, 01108
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/bright-nights-at-forest-park-2/
END:VEVENT
