DESCRIPTION:The Annual Lighting of the Merry Maple on the Amherst Town Com
 mons. FREE event – OPEN to all! Join the community for a magical evening
  as the Town Common sparkles to life and downtown becomes a winter wonderl
 and. Savor music\, warm drinks\, and the joyful countdown to the tree ligh
 ting\, then linger for photos\, window shopping\, and family friendly acti
 vities that keep the holiday spirit glowing. The tree illumination is only
  one part of the merriest downtown Amherst events on Friday. Join us for t
 he festivities from 3-6PM and then after\, enjoy all that downtown has to 
 offer! Shop\, eat\, and experience the heart of Amherst freshly decorated 
 as a winter wonderland! The 50-plus-year-old tradition of lighting a livin
 g tree in the North Common was first documented in print in the Amherst Re
 cord in 1966. Prior to that a Christmas tree was brought in to be decorate
 d and lit.\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewe
 sternmass.com/event/amherst-merry-maple/
