DTEND:20261204T203000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:58c3b92cbee3c94af36d3af08233f3@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a beginner’s astronomy program featuring a short
  talk by a local expert\, hands-on activities or demonstrations\, a planet
 arium show with our historic Korkosz starball and brand-new Zeiss projecto
 r\, and stargazing in our rooftop observatory. Recommended for ages 8 and 
 older. This Month’s Topic: NASA’s Next Adventure: The Nancy Grace Roma
 n Telescope The Nancy Grace Roman Space Telescope launched at the end of A
 ugust and is getting ready to send back rich\, new\, beautiful images that
  change what we know about our cosmos! Join us for an overview of what thi
 s amazing telescope has taught us so far! Reservations Required! Register 
 Now Visit the Springfield Stars club website. The Springfield Museums and 
 the Springfield STARS Club present Stars Over Springfield \, at the Spring
 field Science Museum. Events continue on the first Friday of each month. A
 dmission is $5 for Museum and STARS Club members and $7 for nonmembers (re
 commended for ages 8 and up).\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page
 : https://explorewesternmass.com/event/springfield-museums-stars-over-spri
 ngfield-2/
LOCATION:Springfield Museums\, 21 Edwards Street\, Springfield\, MA\, 0110
 3
