BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:(start)over by Jessica Algard
DTSTART:20261204T193000
DTEND:20261204T210000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:72461d919ef5bfddfeaa85d8bf58d7@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Young Woman has just moved to a new city where she is going to
  start a new job\, make new friends and begin a NEW phase in her long-term
  relationship. The world is full of possibilities—and that’s really sc
 ary! Young Woman\, with the misguided help of her Gaggle (a trio of figure
 s that appear from her moving boxes)\, tries to start her life over. Can s
 he live up to her boss’s expectations? Will anyone want to be her friend
 ? Does she want to marry Young Man? Will she ever unpack all her boxes?! (
 start)over is a look at life in your 20s\, when everything is constantly c
 hanging\, for the better and worse. This play rushes through time and mixe
 s the mundane with the momentous to recreate the feeling of those tumultuo
 us years and all the ways we try to talk ourselves through them. Performin
 g December 4th to 6th\, all performances are at The Natti-Willsky Performa
 nce Center\, Home of Gloucester Stage Company\, 267 East Main Street\, Glo
 ucester. Showtimes are Friday & Saturday at 7:30pm and Sunday at 2:00pm. T
 ickets can be purchased online or by calling the box office at 978-281-443
 3.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/even
 t/startover-by-jessica-algard/2026-12-04/
LOCATION:Natti-Willsky Performance Center: Home of Gloucester Stage Compan
 y\, 267 East Main St.\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/startover-by-jessica-algard/2026-12-04
 /
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Studio Two
DTSTART:20261204T200000
DTEND:20261204T220000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:9e4b68df82406ffb9f4ac1a2171692@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Since 2012\, Studio Two has been passionately bringing the ico
 nic music of early Beatles history back to life. Recreating the raw energy
 \, infectious melodies\, and classic look of 1962-1966\, this Boston-based
  band faithfully captures the legendary foundation of the Fab Four. From t
 he raucous nights at Liverpool’s Cavern Club to the hysterical heights o
 f Beatlemania on American shores\, Studio Two delivers a high-energy\, per
 iod-accurate performance that keeps audiences on their feet. Packed with m
 op-top magic\, youthful charm\, and chart-topping hits\, their family-frie
 ndly show captures the exact sonic drive and Mersey beat that revolutioniz
 ed pop music. Step back in time and experience Beatlemania the way it swep
 t the world-live\, loud\, and unforgettable. Thelarcom.org/studiotwo\n\nSo
 urces: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/studio
 -two-5/
LOCATION:Larcom Theatre\, 13 Wallis Street\, Beverly\, MA\, 01915
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/studio-two-5/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Irish Tenors at HOPE Center for the Arts
DTSTART:20261204T190000
DTEND:20261204T210000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:9683d37c4bac99176ef7af599f51dd@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:For more than a quarter century\, The Irish Tenors have thrill
 ed audiences around the world with their unmistakable blend of soaring cla
 ssical voices\, Irish charm\, and heartfelt storytelling. Since first join
 ing voices in 1998\, they have sold out iconic venues including Radio City
  Music Hall\, Carnegie Hall\, the Sydney Opera House\, and The Hollywood B
 owl\, while becoming beloved PBS favorites through acclaimed specials such
  as Ellis Island . With millions of albums sold and a repertoire that effo
 rtlessly spans treasured Irish ballads\, popular standards\, and stirring 
 contemporary favorites\, The Irish Tenors have become one of the most succ
 essful Irish touring acts in the world. This December\, they return with T
 he Irish Tenors: A Family Christmas \, a holiday celebration that has beco
 me a cherished tradition for audiences across the country. Featuring belov
 ed Christmas classics\, inspirational seasonal favorites\, and the rich ha
 rmonies that made their We Three Kings holiday album a perennial favorite
 \, this festive program captures both the joy and reverence of the season.
  Expect an evening filled with warmth\, laughter\, nostalgia\, and the unm
 istakable magic of holiday music shared with the people you love. Led by t
 he extraordinary voices of Anthony Kearns\, Ronan Tynan\, and Patrick Hyla
 nd\, The Irish Tenors bring dazzling vocal power\, emotional depth\, and a
  touch of Irish sparkle to every performance. Whether delivering the spine
 -tingling beauty of “Danny Boy\,” the festive exuberance of Christmas 
 favorites\, or uplifting songs that bring audiences to their feet\, their 
 concerts are unforgettable celebrations of music\, memory\, and togetherne
 ss. Gather the whole family and make this spectacular holiday event part o
 f your Christmas tradition. TICKETS\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEven
 t page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event/the-irish-tenors-at-hope-cent
 er-for-the-arts/
LOCATION:Hope Center for the Arts\, 150 Bridge Street\, Springfield\, MA\,
  01103
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/the-irish-tenors-at-hope-center-f
 or-the-arts/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tom Hambridge Out Front at 52 Sumner
DTSTART:20261204T193000
DTEND:20261204T220000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:a9858bb7276c4e7a7a133205e3a2b9@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Tom Hambridge is a 5-time Grammy-winning singer\, songwriter\,
  producer & drummer. Tom has produced over 100 albums and had over 1000 of
  his songs recorded by artists including: Eric Clapton\, Van Morrison\, ZZ
  Top\, Mick Jagger\, Gregg Allman\, Keith Richards\, BB King\, James Taylo
 r\, Peter Frampton\, Joe Walsh\, Lynyrd Skynyrd\, Johnny Winter\, Keith Ur
 ban\, Carlos Santana\, Jeff Beck\, George Thorogood\, Joss Stone\, Gary Cl
 ark Jr.\, Warren Haynes\, Joe Bonamassa\, Foghat\, Meatloaf\, Mavis Staple
 s\, Allen Toussaint\, Christone “Kingfish” Ingram\, Jason Isbell\, Jam
 es Bay\, Susan Tedeschi\, James Cotton\, Keb Mo’\, Rascal Flatts\, Steve
 n Tyler\, Delbert McClinton\, John Mayall\, NRBQ and many others. Tom’s 
 songs have been included in many major motion pictures\, TV movies and sho
 ws from American Idol\, Criminal Minds to The Super Bowl. Tom has had 100 
 of his songs recorded by Buddy Guy alone. Tom has produced 15 Grammy nomin
 ated albums\, won Five Grammy’s\, won countless Handy and Blues Awards\,
  ASCAP Country Music Awards and Boston Music Awards. He is a recipient of 
 the prestigious KBA Award in Memphis (Keeping the Blues Alive) and has bee
 n inducted into the Buffalo Music Hall Of Fame. As an artist Tom has relea
 sed 9 solo albums including his latest “Down The Hatch” in 2025 which 
 spent 14 weeks at Number 1 on the Roots Music Report- Blues Rock Album Cha
 rts and has spent 6 months in the Top Ten on The Living Blues Album Charts
 ! Tom also toured for years as musical director/drummer for: Chuck Berry\,
  Buddy Guy\, Bo Diddley and Roy Buchanan TICKETS\n\nSources: Explore Weste
 rn Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event/tom-hambridge-ou
 t-front-at-52-sumner/
LOCATION:52 Sumner\, 52 Sumner Avenue\, Springfield\, MA\, 01108
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/tom-hambridge-out-front-at-52-sum
 ner/
END:VEVENT
