SUMMARY:Springfield Museums\, Class
DTSTART:20261205T103000
DTEND:20261205T123000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:22cfc90eb6fb56cfa5f6b29092c0a0@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Straw Art Holiday Traditions December 5 @ 10:30 am – 12:30 p
 m Register | Cost: $28 | Cost for Members: $24 In this 2-hour class\, part
 icipants can create straw art pictures or cards\, or make a hanging decora
 tion. Straw art pictures are traditionally created in China\, India\, Russ
 ia\, Serbia\, Eastern Europe\, and Scandinavia\, although not always in re
 lation to Christmas. Eastern European countries and Scandinavia are more s
 pecifically related to straw art holiday traditions and include a wide arr
 ay of holiday cards and pictures. Samples will be available for participan
 ts to develop their ideas. Cards and pictures are created from wheat straw
  that is boiled\, ironed\, flattened\, glued to backing and cut into desig
 ns. Hanging decorations are traditionally made from wheat straw that is pr
 e-soaked or boiled and sewn together to create both 2D and 3D forms. Hangi
 ng decorations can also be made from commercial straw if participants pref
 er\, as it is does not require any preparation and is easier to sew. Instr
 uctor: Susan Urban Saturday\, 10:30 am-12:30 pm One class: December 5\n\nS
 ources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.com/e
 vent/springfield-museums-class/
LOCATION:Springfield Museums\, 21 Edwards Street\, Springfield\, MA\, 0110
 3
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/springfield-museums-class/
END:VEVENT
