BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stockbridge Main Street at Christmas
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261205
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261207
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:7b4c4ea8f66ab49b48a5797ee4a8aa@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Norman Rockwell Museum will help celebrate the Annual Stockbri
 dge Main Street at Christmas The town of Stockbridge\, made famous by Norm
 an Rockwell’s painting of the village during the holidays\, becomes a ma
 gical New England setting decorated with holiday wreaths and festive light
 s. SATURDAY Take a guided walking tour of downtown Stockbridge during THE 
 37th ANNUAL STOCKBRIDGE MAIN STREET AT CHRISTMAS Weekend . D iscover how t
 he town and its inhabitants both inspired Norman Rockwell and appeared in 
 some of his most iconic works of art. Explore the history of this 1734 vil
 lage–including its Mohican origins. Stops will include Norman Rockwell
 ’s home on South Street\, his first studio on Main Street\, the Old Corn
 er House (site of the original Norman Rockwell Museum)\, Chief John Konkap
 ot’s property\, the Red Lion Inn\, the former site of Alice’s Restaura
 nt\, and more! Limited capacity- advance reservations required. Tours at 1
 0:30 am\, 12\, and 2 pm Meet in front of The Old Corner House\, 48 Main St
 reet\; public on street parking. Tours start promptly at the designated ti
 me\, please allow ample time for parking. Tour route is mostly flat\, and 
 on sidewalks. Buy Tickets $20\; separate from Museum Admission Tours at 10
 :30 am\, 12\, and 2 pm These tours do not take place at the Museum. Tour g
 roups will meet on Main Street. Transportation to Main Street from the Mus
 eum is not provided. SUNDAY Stockbridge Main Street at Christmas Recreatio
 n ~ 12 Noon-2:00pm The weekend culminates on Sunday with Stockbridge’s b
 eloved Main Street at Christmas Recreation\, inspired by Norman Rockwell
 ’s iconic painting Home for Christmas . With Main Street closed to traff
 ic\, more than 25 vintage automobiles line the street\, recreating the cha
 rm of a bygone era (weather permitted). A beautifully decorated Christmas 
 tree fills the oversized window of Rockwell’s former studio\, while Vict
 orian carolers and students from Monument Mountain Regional High School pr
 ovide festive entertainment. Families can enjoy Roger the Jester\, fire tr
 uck discoveries\, children’s crafts\, and visits with Santa and Mrs. Cla
 us and their reindeer sheep. Stroll along Main Street\, browse local shops
  and the Norman Rockwell Museum pop-up shop\, and enjoy seasonal food and 
 beverages at El Nopal Mexican Cuisine and the Red Lion Inn’s pop-up cour
 tyard booth. This heartwarming tradition offers a wonderful way to celebra
 te the holiday season and experience the timeless charm of Stockbridge. Ad
 mission: $5 per person (includes commemorative button while supplies last)
  | Children under 12: Free PURCHASE TICKETS Horse-drawn wagon rides by Cla
 y Hill Farm will also be available for an additional fee (weather permitti
 ng\; heavy rain cancels rides). *Photo Credit: Norman Rockwell\, Stockbrid
 ge Main Street at Christmas. From the Permanent Collection\, and on view a
 t Norman Rockwell Museum. © 1967\, Norman Rockwell Family Agency The fest
 ivities celebrate Rockwell’s popular depiction of what for many is the q
 uintessential small New England Town\, with all the longing for a simpler 
 time that it represents. Rockwell began painting the popular image in 1956
  but did not complete it until December 1967. The image and character of S
 tockbridge has changed little over the years\, thanks to the great care an
 d affection of its residents\, and it is that special ambience which draws
  so many.\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewes
 ternmass.com/event/stockbridge-main-street-at-christmas/
LOCATION:Norman Rockwell Museum\, 9 Route 183 (Glendale Ave)\, Stockbridge
 \, MA\, 01262
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/stockbridge-main-street-at-christ
 mas/
END:VEVENT
