UID:c5a119842102e2982b4956e4309b64@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Eastern States Exposition presents Yuletide at Storrowton Vill
 age Museum events each year during the first weekend in December with free
  activities and through the following week with paid tours\, workshops and
  lantern light experiences. The winter festival brings the community toget
 her to celebrate the season with traditional Yuletide activities\, enterta
 inment\, trolley rides and shopping in the historic Village. Decorated thr
 ough the generosity of area garden clubs\, florists\, businesses\, school 
 groups\, and designers\, the Village buildings will be bursting with innov
 ative and original ideas to turn your home into a holiday wonderland. Walk
  through the buildings to find beautiful wreaths\, swags\, garlands\, fres
 h evergreens and all natural materials around every corner. Yuletide Event
 s YULETIDE WEEKEND – DECEMBER 5-6 Yuletide Weekend brings the community 
 together to celebrate the season with traditional Yuletide activities\, en
 tertainment\, family fun\, and more. Visitors will enjoy visiting decorate
 d spaces provided by the generosity of area garden clubs and volunteers. F
 ree! A festive\, free weekend of beautifully decorated buildings\, enterta
 inment\, trade demonstrations\, farm animals\, kids activities\, visits wi
 th Santa and Mrs. Claus and so much more! 10am – 4pm. YULETIDE GUIDED TO
 URS – DECEMBER 7-12 Online/Advance: $11 per person\, under 6 free In-per
 son: $13 per person\, under 6 free Create your own Yuletide experience and
  explore the museum’s decorated buildings with a costumed guide during Y
 uletide Open House Tours. Reserve your tour time ahead or drop in on the h
 our from 10am – 3pm. Last tour departs at 3pm. SPIRITS OF CHRISTMAS PAST
  – DECEMBER 5 & DECEMBER 10 $30 per person Enjoy one of Storrowton’s G
 host Tours with a Yuletide twist! Take a tour of Storrowton Village Museum
  & learn about the history of Christmas ghost stories\, unexplained occurr
 ences in the Village\, the dark side of historic winter festivities\, and 
 more! Spirits of Christmas Past tours are on December 5 and 12 at 6pm only
 \, approximately 2 hours long\, and are recommended for ages 12 and up. Ph
 otography will be allowed on certain parts of the tour. No video is allowe
 d. Please check in at the Meeting House where the tour will begin. Dress i
 n layers and wear sensible shoes. Ghost tours are not wheelchair accessibl
 e and include walking up and down stairs. The Gift Shop is always open dur
 ing Museum Tours\, Workshops\, and other public offerings. Plus\, you can 
 enjoy 20% on all purchases at the Christmas Shop during Yuletide! The Farm
 ers Market located near Gate 9 is also open for shopping throughout the ye
 ar\; hours can be found here . Parking is free for all Storrowton events. 
 Activities will take place weather permitting. For more information\, call
  the village at 413-205-5051 or visit us at StorrowtonVillage.com . Try de
 licious regional wines and cheeses or find the perfect handcrafted holiday
  gifts for your loved ones. Stop by the Eastern States Farmers Market Thur
 sday-Saturday 9am-7pm and Sunday 9am-5pm\, and Storrowton Village’s Gift
  & Christmas Shops Thursday-Sunday\, 9am-5pm!\n\nSources: Explore Western 
 Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event/storrowton-village-
 yuletide-at-storrowton/
LOCATION:Storrowton Village at ESE\, 1305 Memorial Avenue\, West Springfie
 ld\, MA\, 01089
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/storrowton-village-yuletide-at-st
 orrowton/
