BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MassMutual Center\, Basketball Hall of Fame Classic
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261206
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261207
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:e7fad3ebe18dde30de7edbe4add08c@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:2026 Basketball Hall of Fame Classic Presented by the Naismith
  Basketball Hall of Fame The Basketball Hall of Fame Classic returns to th
 e MassMutual Center on Sunday\, December 6\, 2026\, bringing an exciting c
 ollege basketball doubleheader to the Birthplace of Basketball. Matchups 
 🏀 UMass vs. Wake Forest – Tip Off 1:00 PM 🏀 Brown vs. Central Conn
 ecticut State University (CCSU) – Tip Off 3:30 PM This year’s event re
 unites UMass and Wake Forest for the first time since 1996\, when future H
 all of Famer Tim Duncan led the Demon Deacons against the Minutemen. Fans 
 can also look forward to a regional rivalry matchup between Brown and CCSU
  as both programs make the trip to downtown Springfield. Hosted in partner
 ship with the Naismith Basketball Hall of Fame\, Explore Western Mass\, an
 d the Springfield Business Improvement District\, the Basketball Hall of F
 ame Classic has become a favorite annual tradition for basketball fans acr
 oss New England. For more information on the Basketball Hall of Fame\, vis
 it Hoophall.com . UMass vs. Wake Forest Series History The Minutemen and D
 emon Deacons have split the two previous matchups. The teams last met 30 y
 ears ago\, with Wake Forest winning 71-47 at home on December 14\, 1996 
 – a game led by future Hall of Famer Tim Duncan. Quotes from Head Coache
 s: “Once again\, we are extremely excited about participating in a Hall 
 of Fame event in Springfield\, Massachusetts. Competing against Wake Fores
 t\, a great member of the ACC\, will be something that will empower our te
 am to grow and give us great visibility.” – Frank Martin | UMass “Ou
 r program is looking forward to the opportunity to play against UMass in t
 he 2026 Basketball Hall of Fame Classic in Springfield\, which celebrates 
 college basketball in the birthplace of this sport. Led by coach Frank Mar
 tin\, UMass is a tradition-rich program and we look forward to the challen
 ge of playing against them on December 6.” – Steve Forbes | Wake Fores
 t CCSU vs. Brown Series History The Bears lead the Blue Devils in their al
 l-time series\, 7-3\, winning seven of the last nine matchups. The teams l
 ast met three years ago\, with Brown winning 59-51 on the road on November
  29\, 2022. Quotes from Head Coaches: “The Basketball Hall of Fame does 
 a great job putting together these events. Playing at the MassMutual Cente
 r will be a positive experience for our program and will be an opportunity
  to play a strong early-season opponent at a neutral site.” – Patrick 
 Sellers | CCSU One Ticket Both Games First Tip Off is at 1:00 PM 🎟️ T
 ickets\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewester
 nmass.com/event/massmutual-center-basketball-hall-of-fame-classic-2/
LOCATION:MassMutual Center\, 1277 Main Street\, Springfield\, MA\, 01103
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/massmutual-center-basketball-hall
 -of-fame-classic-2/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents May Exhibitions at 65 Water Street
DTSTART:20261206T110000
DTEND:20261206T170000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:0114773d1b90b1c83c502d160b203f@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) presents three new shows opening in the 
 month of May! Soft Structures is a group exhibition that explores fibers a
 nd fibrous material as process and metaphor. This exhibit features over 80
  artworks in a variety of media including drawing\, painting\, sculpture\,
  weaving\, embroidery\, quilting\, collage\, mixed media and more. This ex
 hibit is on view in the first-floor Sargent Gallery and second-floor Harts
 on Gallery. FOLIA is a collaborative exhibition featuring works by Amesbur
 y artists Amy Vander Els & Heather Karp. This exhibit explores the quiet b
 eauty and joyful rhythm of leaves and the symbolic meaning behind many tha
 t speaks of perseverance\, resilience and hope. Thirty-six artworks are di
 splayed amongst spring greenery in the first-floor Hills Gallery. Amy and 
 Heather will give a free artist talk on Thursday\, May 21st from 6:00-7:00
 pm\, concluding with Q&A. The 11th Annual Outdoor Sculpture Garden Exhibit
 ion debuted on May 1st\, and will remain on view year-round until April 20
 27. At nearly 3\,000 square feet\, the Range Lights Sculpture Garden resid
 es behind the historic NAA and is seen and visited by hundreds of people e
 very week. This year’s exhibition features 16 pieces by 10 local and reg
 ional artists. The participating artists include\; Jeffrey Briggs\, Lindle
 y Briggs\, Sarah Burns and Mike Platt\, Alexis Guieb-Alimbuyuguen\, Andrew
  Henschel\, Mae Kenny\, Evan Ralph\, Michael Updike and Raynor Warner. A r
 eception for FOLIA and Soft Structures will be held on Saturday\, May 2nd 
 from 4-6pm\, with the 11th Annual Sculpture Exhibit reception beginning at
  3:00pm\, including a Best in Show award at 3:30pm. The receptions are fre
 e and open to the public\, and visitors participating in the May 2nd Newbu
 ryport Artwalk are encouraged to stop by. New Hours: Wednesday through Sun
 day from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More inform
 ation\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. F
 ounded in 1948\, Newburyport Art\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit\, is dedicated t
 o promoting and exhibiting members’ work and to providing art education 
 and access to the visual arts for the entire community. The gallery and ev
 ents are free and open to the public.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent p
 age: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibiti
 ons-at-65-water-street/2026-12-06/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibitio
 ns-at-65-water-street/2026-12-06/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Old Sturbridge Village\, Christmas by Candlelight
DTSTART:20261206T140000
DTEND:20261206T200000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:c4c250089ec0d0678dff5e471321a1@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Experience the timeless charm of Christmas by Candlelight at O
 ld Sturbridge Village. Wander candlelit pathways\, enjoy festive music and
  horse-drawn carryall rides\, discover historic holiday traditions\, savor
  seasonal treats\, explore the Christmas Tree Trail\, and more! November 2
 7 – December 27 (closed Friday\, December 25) Times: 2 – 8 PM GET TICK
 ETS Want to visit multiple times during the holiday season? Consider purch
 asing a Candlelight Club pass – on sale now! Sparkling Sights & Festive 
 Decorations Come see the Village decorated for the season! Glowing lantern
 s and twinkling string lights will guide you as you stroll along the Chris
 tmas Tree Trail and across the Wish Bridge. Every night there will be a li
 ghting ceremony at 4:30 p.m. Plus\, each historical home is adorned for th
 e season inside and out. Cozy Christmas Traditions Discover the origins an
 d evolution of traditions like nutcrackers\, Christmas stockings\, Christm
 as tree ornaments\, Christmas gifts\, teddy bears\, dolls\, and more. Samp
 le sweet treats like mulled cider and gingerbread in select buildings. In 
 the Richardson House\, learn about an assortment of Italian Christmas trad
 itions. See a spectacular miniature nativity featuring 600+ pieces. Explor
 e the history of other winter holidays as well! Merry Music Hear the sound
 s of familiar seasonal songs and sing along! Village favorites such as “
 Up on the Housetop” and others were written in New England in the 1800s.
  Delicious Delights Warm up with cup of soup\, or stew. Relax and treat yo
 urself to a festive hot cocoa\, cider\, or signature drink. Be sure to sav
 e room for\, or plan to take home Village-baked cookies and fudge. Shop fo
 r Unique Gifts From Village-made pottery and tin\, to candy\, spices\, and
  ornaments\, bring home a memory from your visit. Plan to check-off your s
 hopping list as there are many stocking stuffers and unique items to disco
 ver. Ox & Yoke Mercantile\, located right outside the Visitor Center\, ope
 ns at 10:00 a.m. every date of Christmas by Candlelight! Or shop online to
 day for delivery in time for the holidays.\n\nSources: Explore Western Mas
 s\nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event/old-sturbridge-village
 -christmas-by-candlelight/2026-12-06/
LOCATION:Old Sturbridge Village\, 1 Old Sturbridge Village Road\, Sturbrid
 ge\, MA\, 01566
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/old-sturbridge-village-christmas-
 by-candlelight/2026-12-06/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Silver Bell Farm\, Santa Claus
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261206
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261207
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:4608ca22746778abed065a81c77a67@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The Classic Silver Bell Christmas Is Back! This holiday season
 \, families are invited to experience the magic of Silver Bell Farm just l
 ike the early days — cozy\, festive\, and full of holiday spirit. During
  Christmas Tree Season weekends \, you can visit the farm for fresh-cut tr
 ees\, sweet treats\, holiday magic\, and…Santa! No reservations required
 . WHEN YOU CAN SEE SANTA AT THE FARM Santa will begin welcoming guests the
  day after Thanksgiving and will be here each weekend during Christmas Tre
 e Season . 📆 Dates November 27–29 December 5–6 December 12–13 Dec
 ember 19-20 🕙 Santa Visit Hours 9AM–12PM & 1PM–3PM (See weekly sche
 dule for confirmation.) No reservations required. Take your own photos! Sa
 nta breaks for lunch promptly at noon and ends for the day at 3PM. 🕙 Sa
 nta Story Time 12:30PM – 1PM daily No reservations required. Enjoy a sto
 ry with Santa and see his latest gadgets from the North Pole! 🔔 Santa
 ’s daytime schedule may vary and will be posted weekly at the farm and o
 nline. Santa also appears each night during Silver Bell Nights for guests 
 attending the evening light show. MAKE A DAY OF IT Enjoy the full farm exp
 erience while you’re here on the weekends: Fresh-cut Christmas trees Fir
 e pits and s’mores Barrel Train rides (weather permitting & additional c
 harges apply) Decorate-your-own wreaths Bakery treats\, hot cocoa\, and se
 asonal gifts SANTA AT SILVER BELL NIGHTS If you’d like an evening visit 
 with Santa\, you can see him as part of Silver Bell Nights \, our illumina
 ted holiday light show. Tickets are on sale now .\n\nSources: Explore West
 ern Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event/silver-bell-far
 m-santa-claus-3/2026-12-06/
LOCATION:Silver Bell Farm\, 305 Silver Street\, Monson\, MA\, 01057
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/silver-bell-farm-santa-claus-3/20
 26-12-06/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Silver Bell Nights
DTSTART:20261206T163000
DTEND:20261206T200000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:98245a16aa578cab4d703b28e87b14@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Silver Bell Nights: Where holiday traditions shine bright… W
 ander the farm at your own pace during Silver Bell Nights \, Silver Bell F
 arm’s signature holiday light experience\, where festive displays\, seas
 onal activities\, and timeless holiday moments come together for families 
 and friends to enjoy. From cozy spots around the farm to the immersive lig
 ht trail and a visit to the North Pole \, the experience offers something 
 special around every corner. Gather & Enjoy the Farm Before and after the 
 light trail\, guests are invited to explore and enjoy the illuminated farm
  grounds . Play areas\, activity spaces\, gathering spots\, and fire pits 
 are all aglow for the season\, creating a festive place to explore\, relax
 \, and warm up. Visit the goats at Santa’s Barnyard \, browse Santa’s 
 Sleigh Shop gift boutique for ornaments and farm-made candles\, or grab a 
 seasonal treat from the City Sidewalk Café & Bakery . Indoor spaces and p
 lay areas offer a cozy break on colder nights\, fire pits provide a warm p
 lace to pause and enjoy s’mores\, and the Barrel Train runs through the 
 Jingle Bell Junction Play Area when the weather allows. Wander the Light T
 rail The heart of Silver Bell Nights is our ¾-mile illuminated walking tr
 ail \, winding through the gravel paths and carriage roads of the farm. As
  you stroll\, the trail tells the story of a year on the farm — from the
  quiet glow of winter to the fresh colors of spring\, the energy of summer
 \, and the crisp magic of fall — all re-imagined through immersive light
  displays \, interactive moments\, and photo-worthy scenes. Highlights inc
 lude the Peppermint Forest \, our 30 foot Pixel Tree \, Cupid’s Cove \, 
 the Silver Bell Dino Reserve \, glowing light tunnels\, and seasonal scene
 s that change and grow each year. The trail is designed to be enjoyed at y
 our own pace\, making it easy for families of all ages to take it all in. 
 Visit the North Pole Finally\, no Silver Bell Nights experience would be c
 omplete without a visit to the North Pole . Here\, families can meet Santa
  at his Tree Stand every night \, in a welcoming setting that feels straig
 ht out of a holiday story. Whether it’s a quick hello or a special photo
  moment\, this visit is often the highlight of the night for kids and adul
 ts alike\, and a tradition that many families return for year after year. 
 Children will also enjoy our illuminated play areas and unlimited Barrel T
 rain rides (weather permitting). Indulge in festive treats and hot cocoa\,
  available for purchase from the Farm Store Bakery\, Frosty’s Treat Truc
 k\, and our Concessions Window. Silver Bell Nights is more than a light sh
 ow\, it’s a cherished family tradition in the making. Join us for an eve
 ning where the spirit of the season comes to life\, and make memories that
  will last forever. Every Wednesday – Sunday Night\, Closed Thanksgiving
  and Christmas Day TICKETS\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: h
 ttps://explorewesternmass.com/event/silver-bell-nights/2026-12-06/
LOCATION:Silver Bell Farm\, 305 Silver Street\, Monson\, MA\, 01057
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/silver-bell-nights/2026-12-06/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:(start)over by Jessica Algard
DTSTART:20261206T140000
DTEND:20261206T153000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:7c2f58debccc9899bc2314b9f8a764@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Young Woman has just moved to a new city where she is going to
  start a new job\, make new friends and begin a NEW phase in her long-term
  relationship. The world is full of possibilities—and that’s really sc
 ary! Young Woman\, with the misguided help of her Gaggle (a trio of figure
 s that appear from her moving boxes)\, tries to start her life over. Can s
 he live up to her boss’s expectations? Will anyone want to be her friend
 ? Does she want to marry Young Man? Will she ever unpack all her boxes?! (
 start)over is a look at life in your 20s\, when everything is constantly c
 hanging\, for the better and worse. This play rushes through time and mixe
 s the mundane with the momentous to recreate the feeling of those tumultuo
 us years and all the ways we try to talk ourselves through them. Performin
 g December 4th to 6th\, all performances are at The Natti-Willsky Performa
 nce Center\, Home of Gloucester Stage Company\, 267 East Main Street\, Glo
 ucester. Showtimes are Friday & Saturday at 7:30pm and Sunday at 2:00pm. T
 ickets can be purchased online or by calling the box office at 978-281-443
 3.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/even
 t/startover-by-jessica-algard/2026-12-06/
LOCATION:Natti-Willsky Performance Center: Home of Gloucester Stage Compan
 y\, 267 East Main St.\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/startover-by-jessica-algard/2026-12-06
 /
END:VEVENT
