SUMMARY:Captain Elias Davis House Tour
DTSTART:20261211T140000
DTEND:20261211T143000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:db16d16a89c4e253908b5fd6e9e1da@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:What can a house tell us about the people who lived there? Ste
 p inside the Capt. Elias Davis House and discover how architecture\, craft
 smanship\, and everyday objects reveal the lives of one Gloucester family 
 and the changing history of Cape Ann. This docent-led experience invites v
 isitors to look closely at the details that transform a historic building 
 into a story of community\, commerce\, and home.\n\nSources: North of Bost
 on\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/captain-elias-davis-house-
 tour/2026-12-11/
LOCATION:Cape Ann Museum\, 27 Pleasant Street\, Gloucester\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/captain-elias-davis-house-tour/2026-12
 -11/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:John Cafferty and The Beaver Brown Band
DTSTART:20261211T200000
DTEND:20261211T220000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:94c1d975ad19e50ff590600ba94f71@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:18+\, Positive I.D. Required The legendary Rhode Island multi-
 platinum rock’n’roll group John Cafferty & The Beaver Brown Band began
  their career in 1973 and achieved mainstream success in the 1980s with th
 e “Eddie & The Cruisers – Motion Picture Soundtrack”. The hit single
  “ON THE DARK SIDE” held the “#1” position on the Billboard Rock c
 harts and the MTV video charts for five consecutive weeks. The album sold 
 over 3 million copies and was certified triple Platinum by the RIAA. The t
 itle track from the group’s 1985 follow-up album “TOUGH ALL OVER” be
 came their second “#1” single on the Billboard Rock charts and the son
 g “C-I-T-Y” reached the Billboard Top 20. John Cafferty’s solo track
  “HEARTS ON FIRE” was featured in Sylvester Stallone’s film “ROCKY
  IV” and he received his second double Platinum soundtrack award. Over t
 he years John has placed 35 songs in major motion pictures. Today John Caf
 ferty & The Beaver Brown Band continue to tour and bring their exciting li
 ve shows to fans around the world. In 2012 they were inducted into the Rho
 de Island Music Hall Of Fame. 2022 marked the release of John Cafferty & t
 he Beaver Brown Band’s GREATEST HITS on Iconoclassic Records. A comprehe
 nsive collection of all “original recordings” from their hit albums an
 d movie soundtracks. In celebration of their 50 years together John Caffer
 ty & the Beaver Brown Band will be releasing a long awaited album of brand
  new songs in the spring of 2024. The pre-released single “DAY IN THE SU
 N” has received 5 star reviews and is climbing the national classic rock
  radio and streaming charts. It is featured in the new 2024 Peter Farrelly
  film “Ricky Stanicky” starring Zac Efron and John Cena.\n\nSources: N
 orth of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/john-cafferty-
 and-the-beaver-brown-band/
LOCATION:The Cut\, 177 Main Street\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/john-cafferty-and-the-beaver-brown-ban
 d/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MassMutual Center\, Annual Festival of Trees
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261212
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:20ce31de3c23db9e6fd7727cf94bc0@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The Springfield Boys & Girls Club’s Festival of Trees return
 s to the MassMutual Center November 27 through December 13. Discover hundr
 eds of beautifully decorated trees\, enter raffles to win incredible prize
 s\, enjoy family-friendly activities\, visit Santa\, and create lasting ho
 liday memories. Every visit helps support the Springfield Boys & Girls Clu
 b and the young people it serves. Learn more at treeraffle.com. Kicking of
 f the day after Thanksgiving\, the Boys & Girls Clubs of Springfield opens
  the Annual Festival of Trees – open Thursday through Sunday. Presented 
 by the Springfield Boys & Girls Club\, this magical event transforms the M
 assMutual Center Convention Center’s Meeting Rooms into a winter wonderl
 and filled with beautifully decorated trees\, festive cheer\, and holiday 
 spirit. Each dazzling tree is donated by local businesses\, organizations
 \, and individuals\, with proceeds directly supporting programs at the Spr
 ingfield Boys & Girls Club — from after-school enrichment and mentoring 
 to athletics\, arts\, and leadership opportunities for Springfield youth. 
 Come experience the wonder\, support a great cause. Tickets SANTA’S HOUR
 S: Friday- Sunday 12:00 PM – 4:00 PM Children 12 & Under: FREE! FREE ADM
 ISSION TO ALL FRIDAY\, NOVEMBER 27TH. No ticket required.\n\nSources: Expl
 ore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event/massmut
 ual-center-annual-festival-of-trees/2026-12-11/
LOCATION:MassMutual Center\, 1277 Main Street\, Springfield\, MA\, 01103
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/massmutual-center-annual-festival
 -of-trees/2026-12-11/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MGM Springfield\, Roar! Comedy Club
DTSTART:20261211T180000
DTEND:20261211T203000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:a0918344225c92e515efd90c09c4c3@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Justin Silva Friday December 11\, 2026 – 8:00 PM & 10:15 PM 
 Saturday December 12\, 2026 – 8:00 PM & 10:15 PM Justin Silva was born a
 nd raised in New Haven\, CT. He started doing comedy at the age of 21. Pri
 or to comedy\, he was an electrician full-time\, and a server at chili’s
  part-time. The workforce was not working out for him. After his first com
 edy show\, he learned it was where he belonged. Justin fell in love with b
 eing on the stage and making people laugh. A year and a half later\, he qu
 it his jobs to pursue his dream. Justin got on stage as much as he could. 
 Attending open mics. Performing for free at comedy shows and accepting hos
 ting gigs for very little to no money. In efforts to share his comedy with
  the world\, he began making content and posting on social media. Buzz\, t
 raffic\, and popularity all grew up and blew up. He decided\, with his fia
 ncé Ashley Cotto it was time to leave Connecticut and take the leap of fa
 ith to move to Florida. Justin continued to grind and work hard every day 
 to become a bigger act. He wants to create people’s favorite space to la
 ugh and is currently touring in a 2024 Worldwide Tour. He believes what yo
 u put in this game is what you get out of it. Justin will continue to put 
 in all that he can\, with great faith that he gets everything he can out o
 f it. Creating content\, performing comedy year-round while providing for 
 his family\, and keeping the faith in making a living\; his 5 children are
  his main inspiration and drive him every day to conquer his dreams. BUY T
 ICKETS MGM Springfield is the place to go for laughs. The unique comedy se
 ries developed by John Tobin Presents\, features an eclectic mix of nation
 ally popular comedians as well as rising industry stars. Upcoming Performa
 nces\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewesternm
 ass.com/event/mgm-springfield-roar-comedy-club-8/2026-12-11/
LOCATION:MGM Springfield\, One MGM Way\, Springfield\, MA\, 01103
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/mgm-springfield-roar-comedy-club-
 8/2026-12-11/
END:VEVENT
