BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Old Sturbridge Village\, Christmas by Candlelight
DTSTART:20261211T140000
DTEND:20261211T200000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:a759e36ee2a59f08b84f04f4521962@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Experience the timeless charm of Christmas by Candlelight at O
 ld Sturbridge Village. Wander candlelit pathways\, enjoy festive music and
  horse-drawn carryall rides\, discover historic holiday traditions\, savor
  seasonal treats\, explore the Christmas Tree Trail\, and more! November 2
 7 – December 27 (closed Friday\, December 25) Times: 2 – 8 PM GET TICK
 ETS Want to visit multiple times during the holiday season? Consider purch
 asing a Candlelight Club pass – on sale now! Sparkling Sights & Festive 
 Decorations Come see the Village decorated for the season! Glowing lantern
 s and twinkling string lights will guide you as you stroll along the Chris
 tmas Tree Trail and across the Wish Bridge. Every night there will be a li
 ghting ceremony at 4:30 p.m. Plus\, each historical home is adorned for th
 e season inside and out. Cozy Christmas Traditions Discover the origins an
 d evolution of traditions like nutcrackers\, Christmas stockings\, Christm
 as tree ornaments\, Christmas gifts\, teddy bears\, dolls\, and more. Samp
 le sweet treats like mulled cider and gingerbread in select buildings. In 
 the Richardson House\, learn about an assortment of Italian Christmas trad
 itions. See a spectacular miniature nativity featuring 600+ pieces. Explor
 e the history of other winter holidays as well! Merry Music Hear the sound
 s of familiar seasonal songs and sing along! Village favorites such as “
 Up on the Housetop” and others were written in New England in the 1800s.
  Delicious Delights Warm up with cup of soup\, or stew. Relax and treat yo
 urself to a festive hot cocoa\, cider\, or signature drink. Be sure to sav
 e room for\, or plan to take home Village-baked cookies and fudge. Shop fo
 r Unique Gifts From Village-made pottery and tin\, to candy\, spices\, and
  ornaments\, bring home a memory from your visit. Plan to check-off your s
 hopping list as there are many stocking stuffers and unique items to disco
 ver. Ox & Yoke Mercantile\, located right outside the Visitor Center\, ope
 ns at 10:00 a.m. every date of Christmas by Candlelight! Or shop online to
 day for delivery in time for the holidays.\n\nSources: Explore Western Mas
 s\nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event/old-sturbridge-village
 -christmas-by-candlelight/2026-12-11/
LOCATION:Old Sturbridge Village\, 1 Old Sturbridge Village Road\, Sturbrid
 ge\, MA\, 01566
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/old-sturbridge-village-christmas-
 by-candlelight/2026-12-11/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Silver Bell Nights
DTSTART:20261211T163000
DTEND:20261211T200000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:99879923da8cfee553ee55a2692002@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Silver Bell Nights: Where holiday traditions shine bright… W
 ander the farm at your own pace during Silver Bell Nights \, Silver Bell F
 arm’s signature holiday light experience\, where festive displays\, seas
 onal activities\, and timeless holiday moments come together for families 
 and friends to enjoy. From cozy spots around the farm to the immersive lig
 ht trail and a visit to the North Pole \, the experience offers something 
 special around every corner. Gather & Enjoy the Farm Before and after the 
 light trail\, guests are invited to explore and enjoy the illuminated farm
  grounds . Play areas\, activity spaces\, gathering spots\, and fire pits 
 are all aglow for the season\, creating a festive place to explore\, relax
 \, and warm up. Visit the goats at Santa’s Barnyard \, browse Santa’s 
 Sleigh Shop gift boutique for ornaments and farm-made candles\, or grab a 
 seasonal treat from the City Sidewalk Café & Bakery . Indoor spaces and p
 lay areas offer a cozy break on colder nights\, fire pits provide a warm p
 lace to pause and enjoy s’mores\, and the Barrel Train runs through the 
 Jingle Bell Junction Play Area when the weather allows. Wander the Light T
 rail The heart of Silver Bell Nights is our ¾-mile illuminated walking tr
 ail \, winding through the gravel paths and carriage roads of the farm. As
  you stroll\, the trail tells the story of a year on the farm — from the
  quiet glow of winter to the fresh colors of spring\, the energy of summer
 \, and the crisp magic of fall — all re-imagined through immersive light
  displays \, interactive moments\, and photo-worthy scenes. Highlights inc
 lude the Peppermint Forest \, our 30 foot Pixel Tree \, Cupid’s Cove \, 
 the Silver Bell Dino Reserve \, glowing light tunnels\, and seasonal scene
 s that change and grow each year. The trail is designed to be enjoyed at y
 our own pace\, making it easy for families of all ages to take it all in. 
 Visit the North Pole Finally\, no Silver Bell Nights experience would be c
 omplete without a visit to the North Pole . Here\, families can meet Santa
  at his Tree Stand every night \, in a welcoming setting that feels straig
 ht out of a holiday story. Whether it’s a quick hello or a special photo
  moment\, this visit is often the highlight of the night for kids and adul
 ts alike\, and a tradition that many families return for year after year. 
 Children will also enjoy our illuminated play areas and unlimited Barrel T
 rain rides (weather permitting). Indulge in festive treats and hot cocoa\,
  available for purchase from the Farm Store Bakery\, Frosty’s Treat Truc
 k\, and our Concessions Window. Silver Bell Nights is more than a light sh
 ow\, it’s a cherished family tradition in the making. Join us for an eve
 ning where the spirit of the season comes to life\, and make memories that
  will last forever. Every Wednesday – Sunday Night\, Closed Thanksgiving
  and Christmas Day TICKETS\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: h
 ttps://explorewesternmass.com/event/silver-bell-nights/2026-12-11/
LOCATION:Silver Bell Farm\, 305 Silver Street\, Monson\, MA\, 01057
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/silver-bell-nights/2026-12-11/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Symphony Hall\, Cinderella
DTSTART:20261211T190000
DTEND:20261211T210000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:35cff58724271d670bb1ebff386ae4@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step into the magical world of Cinderella\, one of the most be
 loved fairytales of all time\, brought to life in a dazzling Broadway-styl
 e ballet production filled with beauty\, humor\, romance\, and unforgettab
 le theatrical magic. This enchanting production by the United European Bal
 let tells the timeless story of a kind and gentle young woman whose courag
 e\, grace\, and belief in love lead her from a life of hardship to a royal
  ball and a dream come true. With expressive choreography\, colorful chara
 cters\, elegant storytelling\, and the unforgettable romance of Cinderella
  and the Prince\, this ballet is a perfect experience for audiences of all
  ages. Set to the magnificent score of Sergei Prokofiev\, one of the great
 est composers of the 20th century\, Cinderella combines classical ballet t
 radition with the charm and excitement of a grand theatrical fairytale. Au
 diences will enjoy elaborate hand-painted sets\, exquisite costumes create
 d by European designers\, and a brilliant cast of international dancers wh
 o bring this beloved story to life with artistry\, emotion\, and grace. Pr
 omoted by Classical Arts Entertainment under the leadership of Michael Art
 \, this family-friendly production invites you to experience the magic of 
 live theater at its finest. Bring your family\, friends\, loved ones\, and
  children\, and enjoy a beautiful evening filled with music\, dance\, laug
 hter\, romance\, and wonder. Cinderella is more than a ballet. It’s a ce
 lebration of dreams\, kindness\, love\, and the belief that magic can happ
 en when the heart stays true. Ballet in two acts with one intermission. Su
 itable for ages 3 and up. BUY TICKETS\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEv
 ent page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event/symphony-hall-cinderella/
LOCATION:Symphony Hall\, 34 Court Street\, Springfield\, MA\, 01103
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/symphony-hall-cinderella/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Thurston Howell
DTSTART:20261211T200000
DTEND:20261211T220000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:ac02ba833d5c144f6bfa78556bef5b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Grab your Piña Colada and set sail on a nostalgic odyssey thr
 ough the smoothest soft rock hits of the ’70s and ’80s—a time when t
 ube socks had stripes\, bikes had banana seats\, and kitchen phones had 20
 -foot curly cords. Get ready for Thurston Howell—Your Premier Yacht Rock
  Spectacular! ​Sing along to chart-topping favorites like “Silly Love 
 Songs” by Paul McCartney & Wings\, “You’re So Vain” by Carly Simon
 \, “What a Fool Believes” by The Doobie Brothers\, “I Can’t Go for
  That” by Hall & Oates\, “Brandy” by Looking Glass\, and “Baby Com
 e Back” by Player—plus unforgettable hits like “Baker Street” by G
 erry Rafferty\, “Ride Like the Wind” by Christopher Cross\, and many m
 ore smooth classics! ​Together\, they have been bringing the smooth soun
 ds of yacht rock to ports along the East Coast—from the rocky\, lobster-
 scented docks of Bar Harbor\, Maine\, all the way down to the sun-soaked\,
  palm-lined marinas of Fort Lauderdale\, Florida. Every harbor. Every suns
 et cruise. Every deck party in between. They were there. They were cool. T
 hey showed up with 100% pure uncut yacht rock…because you can’t fake s
 mooth! Bring your sailor hats and captain’s hats\, gather your crew\, an
 d set sail with Thurston Howell for a Yacht Rock Spectacular. All hands on
  deck! Thelarcom.org/thurstonhowell\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent pag
 e: https://northofboston.org/event/thurston-howell/
LOCATION:Larcom Theatre\, 13 Wallis Street\, Beverly\, MA\, 01915
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/thurston-howell/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tony DeSare: Holiday Pops
DTSTART:20261211T193000
DTEND:20261211T213000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:b708901277f087cab0b74da3b8a1bf@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Tony DeSare delivers a fresh take on the Great American Songbo
 ok\, blending jazz\, swing\, and pop with charm and virtuosity. From Sinat
 ra to Billy Joel\, plus his own award-winning songs\, DeSare’s program c
 elebrates timeless melodies and heartfelt storytelling. A dynamic evening 
 of all your holiday favorites with one of today’s most engaging performe
 rs. ABOUT THE ARTIST Tony DeSare performs with infectious joy\, wry playfu
 lness and robust musicality. Named “Rising Star Male Vocalist” in Down
 beat magazine\, DeSare has lived up to this distinction by winning critica
 l and popular acclaim for his concert performances throughout North Americ
 a and abroad. From jazz clubs to Carnegie Hall to Las Vegas and headlining
  major symphony orchestras\, DeSare has brought his fresh take on old scho
 ol class around the globe. DeSare has four top ten Billboard jazz albums u
 nder his belt and has been featured on the CBS Early Show\, NPR\, A Prairi
 e Home Companion\, and the Today Show\, and his music has been posted by s
 ocial media celebrity juggernaut George Takei. DeSare has also collaborate
 d with YouTube supergroup Postmodern Jukebox. He has been a featured guest
  artist with over 100 symphony orchestras with some highlights including t
 he Cleveland Orchestra\, The New York Pops\, The San Francisco Symphony\, 
 The Houston Symphony\, and the Chicago Symphony. Notwithstanding his criti
 cally acclaimed turns as a singer/pianist\, DeSare is also an award-winnin
 g composer. He not only won first place in the USA Songwriting Contest\, b
 ut has written the theme song for the motion picture My Date With Drew and
  several broadcast commercials\, and has scored five films. His sound is r
 omantic\, swinging\, and sensual\, but what sets DeSare apart is his abili
 ty to write original material that sounds fresh and contemporary\, yet pay
 s homage to the Great American Songbook. Tony has a strong presence on soc
 ial media and continues to release his “song diaries\,” recordings fro
 m his home studio that started in 2020 and now number in the 100s. Tony ha
 s numerous recordings available on all platforms and playlists. Tony DeSar
 e is a Yamaha Artist.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://nor
 thofboston.org/event/tony-desare-holiday-pops-2/
LOCATION:Shalin Liu Performance Center\, 37 Main Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 
 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/tony-desare-holiday-pops-2/
END:VEVENT
