BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Silver Bell Nights
DTSTART:20261212T163000
DTEND:20261212T200000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:f0c2312fd8a4b96c491577746d69ba@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Silver Bell Nights: Where holiday traditions shine bright… W
 ander the farm at your own pace during Silver Bell Nights \, Silver Bell F
 arm’s signature holiday light experience\, where festive displays\, seas
 onal activities\, and timeless holiday moments come together for families 
 and friends to enjoy. From cozy spots around the farm to the immersive lig
 ht trail and a visit to the North Pole \, the experience offers something 
 special around every corner. Gather & Enjoy the Farm Before and after the 
 light trail\, guests are invited to explore and enjoy the illuminated farm
  grounds . Play areas\, activity spaces\, gathering spots\, and fire pits 
 are all aglow for the season\, creating a festive place to explore\, relax
 \, and warm up. Visit the goats at Santa’s Barnyard \, browse Santa’s 
 Sleigh Shop gift boutique for ornaments and farm-made candles\, or grab a 
 seasonal treat from the City Sidewalk Café & Bakery . Indoor spaces and p
 lay areas offer a cozy break on colder nights\, fire pits provide a warm p
 lace to pause and enjoy s’mores\, and the Barrel Train runs through the 
 Jingle Bell Junction Play Area when the weather allows. Wander the Light T
 rail The heart of Silver Bell Nights is our ¾-mile illuminated walking tr
 ail \, winding through the gravel paths and carriage roads of the farm. As
  you stroll\, the trail tells the story of a year on the farm — from the
  quiet glow of winter to the fresh colors of spring\, the energy of summer
 \, and the crisp magic of fall — all re-imagined through immersive light
  displays \, interactive moments\, and photo-worthy scenes. Highlights inc
 lude the Peppermint Forest \, our 30 foot Pixel Tree \, Cupid’s Cove \, 
 the Silver Bell Dino Reserve \, glowing light tunnels\, and seasonal scene
 s that change and grow each year. The trail is designed to be enjoyed at y
 our own pace\, making it easy for families of all ages to take it all in. 
 Visit the North Pole Finally\, no Silver Bell Nights experience would be c
 omplete without a visit to the North Pole . Here\, families can meet Santa
  at his Tree Stand every night \, in a welcoming setting that feels straig
 ht out of a holiday story. Whether it’s a quick hello or a special photo
  moment\, this visit is often the highlight of the night for kids and adul
 ts alike\, and a tradition that many families return for year after year. 
 Children will also enjoy our illuminated play areas and unlimited Barrel T
 rain rides (weather permitting). Indulge in festive treats and hot cocoa\,
  available for purchase from the Farm Store Bakery\, Frosty’s Treat Truc
 k\, and our Concessions Window. Silver Bell Nights is more than a light sh
 ow\, it’s a cherished family tradition in the making. Join us for an eve
 ning where the spirit of the season comes to life\, and make memories that
  will last forever. Every Wednesday – Sunday Night\, Closed Thanksgiving
  and Christmas Day TICKETS\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: h
 ttps://explorewesternmass.com/event/silver-bell-nights/2026-12-12/
LOCATION:Silver Bell Farm\, 305 Silver Street\, Monson\, MA\, 01057
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/silver-bell-nights/2026-12-12/
END:VEVENT
