SUMMARY:Bright Nights at Forest Park\, Supper with Santa
DTSTART:20261213T173000
DTEND:20261213T190000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:4a84543b0eb6c459c18cfef43068c6@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Supper with Santa is a special night of Bright Nights combined
  with a family-friendly dinner with the big man in the red suit at the his
 toric Barney Carriage House. Every child is going to leave with a big smil
 e\, memories to share\, and a souvenir “I had Supper with Santa” mug. 
 The dinners on Sunday\, December 6th\, Friday\, December 11th\, and Sunday
 \, December 13th feature a table set for each reservation\, and an extra c
 hair for Santa. The buffet menu includes a winter salad with cranberry vin
 aigrette\, macaroni and cheese\, chicken tenders with sauces\, ziti marina
 ra\, breadsticks\, rolls\, hot chocolate\, juice boxes\, coffee\, and tea.
  For dessert\, there are scrumptious Christmas cookies and brownies. Ticke
 ts are $30 each. Children under 12 are $15 each\, and children under 2 are
  free. Tickets are purchased online at brightnights.org . Paid reservation
 s receive ONE complimentary Bright Nights at Forest Park vehicle admission
 . If additional tickets are required for the reservation\, they are availa
 ble at $15 each plus $2 ticket fee. RESERVATIONS Personal cameras are welc
 ome so you can capture the moment. Seatings 5:30PM 6:00PM 6:30PM 7:00PM Br
 ight Nights Named Best of the Best Since 1995\, Bright Nights has been a u
 nique public/private collaboration between the City of Springfield’s Dep
 artment of Parks\, Buildings & Recreation Management and the Spirit of Spr
 ingfield\, a private non-profit organization. Together they have welcomed 
 more than 6 million visitors. It has been calculated that if every bus tha
 t had visited were lined bumper to bumper\, they would go from Springfield
  to Cape Cod. The cars would go as far as California. BUY TICKETS\n\nSourc
 es: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event
 /bright-nights-at-forest-park-supper-with-santa-3/
LOCATION:Forest Park\, 300 Sumner Avenue\, Springfield\, MA\, 01108
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/bright-nights-at-forest-park-supp
 er-with-santa-3/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Growing Together: Natural Holiday Gifts from the Garden
DTSTART:20261213T100000
DTEND:20261213T120000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:1ee554c658ef9491a0ee39ca935b11@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Turn the garden’s bounty into thoughtful\, handmade gifts fo
 r the holiday season. This hands-on workshop explores creative ways to use
  dried herbs\, flowers\, seeds\, and other garden-grown materials to make 
 simple\, beautiful gifts such as garden-inspired sugar scrubs\, botanical 
 sachets\, infused salts\, tea mixes\, and natural decorations. Participant
 s will leave with inspiration and handmade creations to share with family 
 and friends. Growing Together is a new hands-on gardening series created i
 n collaboration with Arianna Iappini of Birch Arbor Gardens. Designed for 
 gardeners of all experience levels\, this series invites participants to l
 earn\, connect\, and cultivate alongside one another through the seasons. 
 Each session blends practical instruction with thoughtful conversation\, e
 xploring sustainable gardening practices\, seasonal rhythms\, and the deep
 er relationships between plants\, place\, and people. Rooted in community 
 and shared knowledge\, Growing Together offers a welcoming space to grow s
 kills\, confidence\, and connection in the historic gardens. Space is limi
 ted—pre-registration is required for this event. This program is rain or
  shine! In the event of cancellation\, you will be notified via the email 
 address you used to register and refunded in full within 14 business days.
  Tickets are non-transferable and non-refundable. Membership: To locate in
 formation about your Membership\, including Member ID\, expiration date\, 
 and more please visit: https://explore.thetrustees.org/manage. Tickets: To
  look up your tickets or re-send an email confirmation\, please visit: htt
 ps://explore.thetrustees.org/order-lookup.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEv
 ent page: https://northofboston.org/event/growing-together-natural-holiday
 -gifts-from-the-garden/
LOCATION:Stevens-Coolidge House &amp\; Gardens\, 153 Chickering Road\, Nor
 th Andover\, MA\, 01845
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/growing-together-natural-holiday-gifts
 -from-the-garden/
END:VEVENT
