BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artful Conversations: Conversations between Regionalism and Modern
 ism
DTSTART:20261217T123000
DTEND:20261217T133000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:c0a83514ebb87416006a02c8d337ed@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join Us Mid-Day for Artful Conversations Take a midday pause a
 nd experience one work of art in depth. Artful Conversations are informal
 \, docent-led gallery experiences that invite visitors to slow down\, look
  closely\, and engage in thoughtful conversation. Each session features a 
 work of art or object that is new to view—whether a recent acquisition o
 r a work newly installed in the galleries. The program begins in the Educa
 tion Room at our Downtown Campus with a brief introduction and visual cont
 ext before moving into the galleries for an extended exploration of the fe
 atured work. Guided by observation\, curiosity\, and conversation\, partic
 ipants are encouraged to share ideas\, consider different perspectives\, a
 nd discover new connections together. This week for Artful Conversations J
 oin us in exploring the dynamic crossroads of American Modernism and Ameri
 can Regionalism—two movements that shaped the artistic identity of Cape 
 Ann. Using a sketch made by Stuart Davis\, Sketch–Church Tower (1916) an
 d Gifford Beal’s Sword Fisherman (1930) as vivid touchpoints\, we’ll d
 ive into how artists responded to sweeping cultural change after World War
  I\, when Modernists embraced bold experimentation and broke from traditio
 nal representation. We’ll also trace the rise of Regionalism during the 
 Great Depression\, when many painters turned toward detailed\, narrative s
 cenes of rural life and local character. This conversation will illuminate
  the tension between these movements\, their relevance to Cape Ann’s art
 istic legacy\, and the enduring impact they continue to have on how we see
  and interpret American art. Along with being a docent at the Cape Ann Mus
 eum\, Tobi Klein is a mixed media artist living and working in Rockport\, 
 MA. Upon receiving an MFA\, Tobi taught painting and drawing at Rochester 
 Institute of Technology. After moving to Boston\, she managed a gallery fo
 r contemporary crafts while\, at the same time\, running a successful smal
 l business. Tobi also worked with elementary school teachers in Arlington
 \, MA\, implementing curriculum-based art projects at her daughter’s sch
 ool. She volunteered in classrooms on a regular basis\, putting an emphasi
 s on group dynamic skills. Life events and a move to Cape Ann motivated he
 r to rediscover her artistic\, creative self. She is revisiting her love o
 f building layers through experimentation with varied materials and techni
 ques. As she learned about the art\, history\, and culture of Cape Ann\, T
 obi wanted to be part of this inspiring and unique region and its Museum. 
 This led her to the Cape Ann Museum docent program – where learning neve
 r ends!\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org
 /event/artful-conversations-conversations-between-regionalism-and-modernis
 m/2026-12-17/
LOCATION:Cape Ann Museum\, 27 Pleasant Street\, Gloucester\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/artful-conversations-conversations-bet
 ween-regionalism-and-modernism/2026-12-17/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
