BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Will Evans with Steve Rondo
DTSTART:20270130T200000
DTEND:20270130T220000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:2a9a38fa070dc0872e9b728c438ffe@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Will Evans creates music as an open invitation—to drop your 
 guard\, tune in\, and move through the world a little more freely. Rooted 
 in folk tradition yet unconfined by genre\, his songs blend thoughtful\, q
 uotable lyrics with sunlit grooves and global textures\, encouraging liste
 ners to reconnect with their most honest selves. Based in Rhode Island\, t
 he singer\, songwriter\, and multi-instrumentalist has built a devoted fol
 lowing by pairing sound with intention\, most notably through his Kind Fol
 k community\, which turns shows into shared experiences of kindness\, char
 ity\, and collective uplift. Known for his dynamic live performances\, Eva
 ns weaves together acoustic guitar\, handpan\, didgeridoo\, beatboxing\, a
 nd percussion to create a fluid\, organic sound that feels both grounded a
 nd expansive. His 2025 release The Wild Unknown pushes that vision further
 \, exploring the crossroads of contemporary folk\, electronica\, and rock
 \, with collaborations from artists like Tristan Prettyman\, Dirtwire\, an
 d Moontricks. From sold-out rooms across the U.S. and Europe to stages sha
 red with Crosby & Nash\, Grace Potter\, Bruce Hornsby\,Dirtwire\, Trevor H
 all\, and Railroad Earth\, Will Evans continues to build a musical space w
 here connection comes first—and everyone belongs. Steve Rondo has built 
 a following across the Northeast\, touring beach towns\, dive bars\, and r
 egional festivals. Songs like Flowers of La Jolla and Afternoon Rebellion 
 showcase his blend of heartfelt storytelling and guitar-driven arrangement
 s — music made for long drives and reflection. A surfer at heart\, Rondo
  brings coastal atmosphere into his songwriting. His songs mirror the ocea
 n’s push and pull — building into anthemic choruses before settling in
 to calm. Themes of freedom\, uncertainty\, and searching for direction run
  throughout his work\, capturing the feeling of chasing waves and dreams. 
 Live\, Rondo and his band balance raw emotion with communal energy. Highli
 ghts include opening for Dermot Kennedy in Portland\, Maine in 2022\, plus
  performances at Levitate Music Festival and 92.5 The River’s Riverfest
 \, cementing their reputation as a rising live act in the region.\n\nSourc
 es: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/will-evan
 s-with-steve-rondo/
LOCATION:The Cut\, 177 Main Street\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/will-evans-with-steve-rondo/
END:VEVENT
