BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The King’s Singers
DTSTART:20270213T193000
DTEND:20270213T210000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:f675986e28d70d0f084fff9801b5cf@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Peter Hicks\, countertenor | Edward Button\, countertenor | Ju
 lian Gregory\, tenor | Joseph Edwards\, baritone | Nick Ashby\, baritone |
  Piers Connor Kennedy\, bass The King’s Singers have set the gold standa
 rd in a cappella singing on the world’s greatest stages for over fifty y
 ears. They are renowned for their unrivalled technique\, musicianship and 
 versatility\, which stem from both the group’s rich heritage and its dri
 ve to bring an extraordinary range of new and unique works\, collaboration
 s and recordings to life. PROGRAM The Romantic impulse spread like wildfir
 e across Europe during the 19th and early 20th centuries. Lieder\, chanson
 s and part songs–imbued with musical richness–became vehicles for the 
 deepest expressions of human feeling\, desire and fantasy. This program pa
 ys deserved tribute to many of the greatest European composers of Romantic
  vocal music from that time: extraordinary storytellers that include Edwar
 d Elgar and Ralph Vaughan Williams in England\, and Hugo Alfvén in Sweden
 \; Felix and Fanny Mendelssohn and Franz Schubert in Germany\, and Claude 
 Debussy\, Maurice Ravel and Camille Saint-Saëns in France. Tonight\, we w
 ant to honor their collective imagination and brave emotional vulnerabilit
 y by taking you on a magical journey that explores some of their most comp
 elling thoughts on life\, love\, nature\, death\, and even the supernatura
 l.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/even
 t/the-kings-singers/
LOCATION:Shalin Liu Performance Center\, 37 Main Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 
 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/the-kings-singers/
END:VEVENT
