BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Homeschool Adventures: Session 1
DTSTART:20270302T130000
DTEND:20270302T160000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:769c918483422e52ab537355ae72da@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Young explorers are invited to join us in September & October 
 for a 4-part homeschool series that will get them active & moving with nat
 ure adventures\, exercise\, and outdoor skill building. While exploring Ap
 pleton Farms & the Crane Estate\, participants complete active adventures 
 & design challenges that will exercise both their body & mind. Some potent
 ial activities include kayaking\, tide pooling\, wetland exploration\, ori
 enteering\, gardening\, obstacle course design\, and more! This is a drop-
 off program that is open to ages 5-11 and will include small group activit
 ies based on age and peer mentoring opportunities between age groups. The 
 class takes place rain or shine\, with as much time spent outdoors as poss
 ible. Students should arrive dressed for the weather and bring a lunch and
  water bottle. Homeschool Adventures: Session 1- This 4-class series progr
 am takes place on Tuesday afternoons from 1-4pm on September 15\, 22\, 29 
 & October 6. September 15: Tidepool & Shoreline Exploration at the Crane E
 state September 22: Kayaking Adventure at the Crane Estate September 29: P
 onding & Invasive Species Management at Appleton Farms October 6: Obstacle
  Course Design Challenge at Appleton Farms Tuition for the 4 classes is $2
 75 for Trustees Members and $325 for nonmembers. Registration covers all l
 isted session dates.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://nort
 hofboston.org/event/homeschool-adventures-session-1/2027-03-02/
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/homeschool-adventures-session-1/2027-0
 3-02/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Symphony Hall\, Brit Floyd “Animals So”
DTSTART:20270302T193000
DTEND:20270302T220000
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:7b13366350e92b1578f17798295c71@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Brit Floyd\, recognized by Rolling Stone Magazine as “The Wo
 rld’s Premier Pink Floyd Experience”\, is renowned for delivering grou
 ndbreaking\, authentic recreations of Pink Floyd’s legendary sound and v
 isual experiences. Since their inception in Liverpool in 2011\, Brit Floyd
  has established itself as a global phenomenon\, performing over 1\,500 sh
 ows across the globe and consistently captivating audiences at some of the
  world’s most prestigious venues\, including London’s Royal Albert Hal
 l\, Denver’s Red Rocks Amphitheatre\, The Greek Theatre in Los Angeles\,
  Radio City Music Hall in New York City\, and Teatro Antico in Taormina in
  Sicily. The band’s performances are celebrated for their meticulous att
 ention to detail\, featuring an immaculate\, state-of-the-art production t
 hat faithfully emulates Pink Floyd’s iconic soundscapes\, laser shows\, 
 and visual effects inspired by their quintessential catalog. Under the lea
 dership of Musical Director Damian Darlington\, Brit Floyd boasts a talent
 ed lineup of accomplished musicians committed to maintaining the integrity
  and authenticity of Pink Floyd’s legendary music. Brit Floyd’s concer
 ts often feature guest musicians from both Pink Floyd’s and Roger Waters
 ’ studio and touring lineups. Past guest performers include Pink Floyd b
 assist Guy Pratt\, and Pink Floyd backing vocalists Machan Taylor\, Durga 
 McBroom\, and Roberta Freeman\, Pink Floyd saxophonist Scott Page\, and ev
 en Roger Waters’ son and long-time touring keyboardist/Hammond player Ha
 rry Waters\, and Roger Waters’ touring and studio drummer Graham Broad. 
 The band has also collaborated on tours and shows with producer icon and r
 ecording artist Alan Parsons\, along with his lead vocalist\, PJ Olsson. T
 his fusion of talented artists and the band’s dedication to quality has 
 earned Brit Floyd a reputation as one of the most authentic and impressive
  tribute experiences in the world. Beyond their musical excellence\, Brit 
 Floyd’s performances are a visual spectacle\, combining stunning lightin
 g\, pyrotechnics\, and visuals\, creating a mesmerizing experience that ho
 nors Pink Floyd’s innovative spirit and legacy. Their dedication to recr
 eating the magic of Pink Floyd has made them a favorite among fans and cri
 tics alike\, solidifying their position as the ultimate tribute act and a 
 celebration of musical and visual artistry. Buy Tickets\n\nSources: Explor
 e Western Mass\nEvent page: https://explorewesternmass.com/event/symphony-
 hall-brit-floyd-animals-so/
LOCATION:Symphony Hall\, 34 Court Street\, Springfield\, MA\, 01103
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/symphony-hall-brit-floyd-animals-
 so/
END:VEVENT
