DESCRIPTION:Join us for the area’s best homecoming celebration. The St. 
 Patrick’s Day celebrations of the 50th Annual St. Patrick’s 10k Road R
 ace on Saturday\, followed by the 74th Holyoke St. Patrick’s Parade on S
 unday. 10K RACE BEGINS Time: 1:00pm Location: Beginning of Maple Street TH
 E WALK The walk will be 2 miles long and start directly after the runners 
 depart. Walkers will go out to the first Mile Marker and the course will c
 ircle them back onto Maple Street and finish at Dwight and Maple. There wi
 ll be entertainment along the walk course. Walkers price also includes a T
 -Shirt. KIDS FUN RUN (No applications or registration needed – This race
  is FREE!!) Line-up: 10:45am (Note: Time change) Start: 11:00am Race Locat
 ion: Intersection of Hampden and Walnut Streets and go through FINISH line
  Groups Line-up: Boys / Girls Ages: | 2 – 4 | 4 – 6 | 6 – 8 | 8 – 
 10 Saturday: Kids Fun Run The intersection of Hampden Street and Walnut St
 reet Holyoke\, MA 01040 Line up: 10:45 am Race: 11:00 am The Expandable Br
 ass Band Parade and Concert with the Colleens The intersection of Maple St
 reet and Hampden Street Holyoke\, MA 01040 12:00 pm Annual Holyoke St. Pat
 rick’s 10K Road Race The intersection of Maple Street and Lyman Street H
 olyoke\, MA 01040 1:00 pm Holyoke St. Patrick’s Road Race 2-Mile Walk Th
 e intersection of Maple Street and Lyman Street Holyoke\, MA 01040 Directl
 y following 10k runners Laying of the Wreath Ceremony at JFK Memorial JFK 
 Memorial Plaza The intersection of Appleton Street and Sycamore Street Hol
 yoke\, MA 01040 4:15 pm A FREE SHUTTLE SERVICE WILL BE RUNNING FROM HOLYOK
 E COMMUNITY COLLEGE TO THE ROAD RACE STARTING AREA. First Shuttle: 9:00 am
  Last Shuttle: 5:00 pm\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https
 ://explorewesternmass.com/event/holyoke-st-patricks-day-road-race-4/
