BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Big E!!
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270917
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271004
DTSTAMP:20261027T170709Z
UID:746155dd36d92152cc021b49474517@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The Big E returns Sept. 17-Oct. 3\, 2027! Guests will be able 
 to visit the Avenue of States\, Storrowton Village Museum\, shop\, eat ico
 nic fair foods\, watch the new Big Parade\, ride the rides and much more. 
 The Big E is the largest event on the East Coast and the fourth largest fa
 ir in North America. Attendees can enjoy hours of free entertainment and a
 ttractions\, terrific food\, plus the best that New England—and beyond
 —has to offer. Highlights include authentic New Orleans Mardi Gras in Th
 e Big Parade\, an immersive Ireland adventure in the International Plaza
 ’s Dingle Peninsula Showcase\, North American Midway\, as well as countl
 ess educational opportunities from the Avenue of States to Storrowton Vill
 age Museum\, Farm-A-Rama and more. The Big E offers a diverse and vibrant 
 experience to visitors from throughout the country. SHOP ‘TIL YOU DROP O
 nly at The Big E can you go home with a set of steak knives\, a hot tub\, 
 a sweater made from Alpaca fiber and maybe even a tractor. With everything
  you could ever want all in one place\, it’s better than any mall in the
  world! GET YOUR “AG” ON! Agriculture is one of Eastern States Exposit
 ion’s oldest traditions and Farm-A-Rama is the heart of agriculture duri
 ng The Big E. Visit the chick hatchery\, pet a goat\, learn about the secr
 et life of bees and all things farm in the Stroh Building. GO BACK IN TIME
  See how 19th century New Englanders lived and worked at Storrowton Villag
 e . Court of Honor Stage You’re not gonna want to miss these concerts at
  The Big E’s Court of Honor Stage! Don’t miss performances that are fr
 ee with admission to the Fair! Lineup The E Stage The E Stage spotlights u
 p-and-coming musicians at The Big E. The venue was developed to showcase e
 merging and regional artists dedicated to creating original music. Catch t
 hese free daily shows! Daily performances will occur at 3 p.m. and 7 p.m. 
 Monday through Thursday and at 12:30 p.m.\, 4:30 p.m. and 8:30 p.m. Friday
  through Sunday during the fair’s 17-day run. Each performance will be a
 n hour-and-a-half long. Lineup Join The Big E’s Mardi Gras Krewe! Mardi 
 Gras Reveler Experience participants will be in the center of the action w
 ith vibrant floats\, costumes\, dazzling lights\, rockin’ tunes\, and TO
 NS of beads at The Big Parade every day at 6pm. Tickets are on sale now! F
 rom Circus Spectacular to The Big Parade \, there’s so much to experienc
 e daily during the Fair! Explore our daily schedule and start planning you
 r visit. Something to Celebrate Every Day From honoring New England’s si
 x states and our neighboring communities\, to spotlighting veterans\, firs
 t responders\, The Big E’s Special and State Day s bring unique energy t
 o the Fair each day. Join us for parades\, ceremonies\, giveaways and them
 ed entertainment that make every visit feel one-of-a-kind. Click here for 
 a schedule of all this year’s Events. Fairtime Hours Gates: 8am The Big 
 E Bakery: 9am–10:30pm Buildings and Craft Common: 10am–10pm Avenue of 
 States: 10am–9pm Storrowton Village Museum & Shops: 10am–9pm New Engla
 nd Center: 10am–9pm Midway: Sunday–Thursday\, 11am–10pm\; Friday–S
 aturday\, 10am–11pm Military Appreciation Day (Sept. 18) ID Required for
  free admission for: • Active duty military personnel and dependents •
  Retired military personnel and Veterans (no dependents) GET TICKETS Pleas
 e note that no weapons are allowed on the grounds. Metal detectors are in 
 use at every entrance gate to the fairgrounds. Bags are subject to search 
 at gates. The Big E Express with PVTA Eastern States Exposition is expandi
 ng transportation options for fairgoers through a new partnership with the
  Pioneer Valley Transit Authority (PVTA)\, throughout all 17 days of The F
 air. PVTA will provide free shuttle service to and from the Fair\, offerin
 g guests an alternative to driving and accessible public transportation. T
 hroughout the run of The Big E\, the PVTA will offer a shuttle service cir
 culating between Springfield’s Union Station\, 55 Frank B Murray Street 
 in Springfield\, Mass.\, and Gate 1 of The Big E fairgrounds on Memorial A
 venue in West Springfield\, Mass.\, serving downtown garages to allow fair
 goers to park downtown and ride to the Fair via PVTA Bus –The Big E Expr
 ess\, or board the shuttle following a train ride\, bus ride or walk to Sp
 ringfield’s Union Station. The Big E Express shuttle will begin Septembe
 r 18\, Opening Day of The Big E\, and continue running daily through Octob
 er 4\, the final day of the Fair. The shuttle offers extended hours\, oper
 ating Monday through Thursday from 1-9pm and Friday\, Saturday\, and Sunda
 y from 10am-10pm. The Big E Express shuttle is made possible by ESE. You c
 an find details about The Big E Express shuttle and PVTA routes via their 
 website\, PVTA.com .\n\nSources: Explore Western Mass\nEvent page: https:/
 /explorewesternmass.com/event/the-big-e/
LOCATION:The Big E\, 1305 Memorial Avenue\, West Springfield\, MA\, 01089
URL:https://explorewesternmass.com/event/the-big-e/
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
